-Great!

94
00:08:14.428 --> 00:08:16.554
Okay, I’ll see you at 7:00.

95
00:08:18.599 --> 00:08:21.559
Jasper, no fair with the mood control thing.

96
00:08:21.644 --> 00:08:22.644
)

97
00:08:23.145 --> 00:08:25.730
Sorry, Bella. Happy...

98
00:08:27.066 --> 00:08:28.441
Never mind.

99
00:08:30.736 --> 00:08:33.988
You can't trust vampires. Trust me.

100
00:08:34.949 --> 00:08:37.033
O my love! My wife!

101
00:08:37.826 --> 00:08:39.994
Death, that hath sucked
the honey of thy breath

102
00:08:40.079 --> 00:08:42.497
hath had no power yet upon thy beauty.

103
00:08:43.666 --> 00:08:45.542
Thou art not conquered.

104
00:08:47.002 --> 00:08:50.922
Beauty's ensign yet is crimson
in thy lips and in thy cheeks.

105
00:08:51.757 --> 00:08:54.592
And death's pale flag is not advanced there.

106
00:08:54.677 --> 00:08:56.636
I hate being celebrated.

107
00:08:57.346 --> 00:09:00.265
There are worse tragedies.
l mean, look at Romeo.

108
00:09:00.349 --> 00:09:03.309
Killed his true love out of sheer stupidity.

109
00:09:05.229 --> 00:09:06.312
Yeah.

110
00:09:06.814 --> 00:09:08.982
Though l do envy him one thing.

111
00:09:10.859 --> 00:09:12.902
Juliet is, like, perfect.

112
00:09:12.987 --> 00:09:16.239
lf you like
that obviously beautiful sort of thing.

113
00:09:19.535 --> 00:09:22.495
Not the girl, the suicide.

114
00:09:26.417 --> 00:09:28.668
It’s nearly impossible for...

115
00:09:30.129 --> 00:09:32.755
For some people.

116
00:09:35.426 --> 00:09:38.678
For humans, a little poison,

117
00:09:40.764 --> 00:09:42.765
a dagger to the heart.

118
00:09:44.059 --> 00:09:46.644
There's so many different options.

119
00:09:49.898 --> 00:09:51.816
Why would you say that?

120
00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:55.612
Because I had to consider it once.

121
00:09:57.823 --> 00:09:59.866
I didn't know if I’d get to you in time.

122
00:10:00.492 --> 00:10:03.661
I had to come up with some kind of plan.

123
00:10:04.913 --> 00:10:06.623
What was the plan?

124
00:10:06.707 --> 00:10:10.168
That I’d go to Italy and provoke the Volturi.

125
00:10:11.003 --> 00:10:13.212
-The what?
-The Volturi.

126
00:10:13.297 --> 00:10:16.758
.  Now, who'd like to repeat
the last few lines of iambic pentameter

127
00:10:16.842 --> 00:10:19.385
just to show they were paying attention?

128
00:10:19.803 --> 00:10:21.220
Mr. Cullen?

129
00:10:24.224 --> 00:10:25.892
Yes, Mr. Berty.

130
00:10:28.604 --> 00:10:32.482
"O here will I set up my everlasting rest

131
00:10:34.485 --> 00:10:38.655
"and shake the yoke of inauspicious stars
from this world-wearied flesh.

132
00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.366
"Eyes, look your last.

133
00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:44.243
"Arms, take your last embrace!

134
00:10:45.204 --> 00:10:48.081
"And, lips, O you, the doors of breath,

135
00:10:48.749 --> 00:10:53.086
"seal with a righteous kiss a dateless
bargain to engrossing death!"

136
00:10:55.339 --> 00:10:57.423
Eyes on the screen, people.

137
00:10:59.093 --> 00:11:01.427
Thus with a kiss I die.

138
00:11:04.765 --> 00:11:08.017
The Volturi are a very old,
very powerful family.

139
00:11:08.602 --> 00:11:12.271
l guess they're the closest thing
to royalty my world has.

140
00:11:12.856 --> 00:11:15.066
-Is that Carlisle?
-Yeah.

141
00:11:16.276 --> 00:11:18.444
He lived with them for a few decades.

142
00:11:18.529 --> 00:11:23.116
Described them as very refined.
No respect for human life, of course,

143
00:11:24.076 --> 00:11:27.495
but a respect for the arts and the sciences,
at least.

144
00:11:29.081 --> 00:11:30.581
And the law.

145
00:11:31.583 --> 00:11:33.334
Above all, the law.

146
00:11:36.588 --> 00:11:38.339
Vampires have laws?

147
00:11:39.883 --> 00:11:41.509
Not very many.

148
00:11:42.678 --> 00:11:45.513
And only one that's regularly enforced.

149
00:11:48.016 --> 00:11:49.475
What is it?

150
00:11:50.561 --> 00:11:53.646
That we keep the existence
of our kind a secret.

151
00:11:54.106 --> 00:11:57.150
We don't make spectacles of ourselves,

152
00:11:59.027 --> 00:12:01.571
and we don't kill conspicuously.

153
00:12:05.492 --> 00:12:07.952
Unless, of course, you want to die.

154
00:12:22.426 --> 00:12:24.427
You gotta stop talking about that.

155
00:12:24.511 --> 00:12:28.306
I can't even think
about someone hurting you.

156
00:12:30.893 --> 00:12:34.979
Bella, the only thing that can hurt me
is you.

157
00:12:37.357 --> 00:12:39.817
And I don't have anything else
to be afraid of.

158
00:12:39.902 --> 00:12:40.985
That's not true.

159
00:12:43.447 --> 00:12:46.199
Victoria? She'll come for me one day.

160
00:12:47.117 --> 00:12:51.621
Alice will see when she decides,
and we'll be ready.

161
00:12:51.872 --> 00:12:53.790
I could protect you

162
00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:56.542
if you change me.

163
00:12:57.211 --> 00:12:59.629
Bella, you already do protect me.

164
00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:03.591
You're my only reason

165
00:13:05.219 --> 00:13:07.011
to stay alive,

166
00:13:07.679 --> 00:13:09.514
if that's what I am.

167
00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:14.143
But it's my job to protect you.

168
00:13:17.731 --> 00:13:20.817
From everyone except my sister.

169
00:13:20.901 --> 00:13:24.111
It’s time! It’s time. It’s time. It’s time!

170
00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:29.617
Your lips are nettles

171
00:13:29.701 --> 00:13:31.744
Your tongue is wine

172
00:13:32.246 --> 00:13:34.831
You're left as liquid
But your body's pine

173
00:13:34.915 --> 00:13:36.582
.  Sorry about all this.

174
00:13:36.667 --> 00:13:39.502
-We tried to rein Alice in.
-As if that were even possible.

175
00:13:39.586 --> 00:13:42.088
-Happy birthday, Bella.
-Thanks.

176
00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:48.010
I found it in your bag. You mind?

177
00:13:48.762 --> 00:13:51.013
Dating an older woman. Hot.

178
00:13:53.225 --> 00:13:55.434
-What?
-You first, Rosalie.

179
00:13:58.313 --> 00:14:01.399
It’s a necklace. Alice picked it out.

180
00:14:01.817 --> 00:14:03.025
Thanks.

181
00:14:05.779 --> 00:14:07.446
Show me the love.

182
00:14:11.159 --> 00:14:13.160
This one's from Emmett.

183
00:14:15.622 --> 00:14:18.124
Already installed it in your truck.

184
00:14:18.208 --> 00:14:19.625
Finally a decent sound system

185
00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:22.086
-for that piece of...
-Hey! Don't hate the truck.

186
00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:23.212
)

187
00:14:23.297 --> 00:14:25.464
Open Esme and Carlisle's.

188
00:14:26.717 --> 00:14:29.218
.  Just a little something
to brighten your day.

189
00:14:29.303 --> 00:14:32.305
Yes, you've been looking
kind of pale lately.

190
00:14:37.561 --> 00:14:38.561
Ow.

191
00:14:40.314 --> 00:14:41.647
Paper cut.

192
00:15:06.381 --> 00:15:09.467
Jaz, Jaz. It’s okay. It’s just a little

193
00:15:11.845 --> 00:15:13.179
blood.

194
00:15:19.686 --> 00:15:21.604
.  Get Jasper out of here.

195
00:15:27.361 --> 00:15:29.654
I’m sorry, I can't.

196
00:15:31.949 --> 00:15:34.742
I’ll have to stitch this up in my office.

197
00:15:37.037 --> 00:15:38.663
Check on Jasper.

198
00:15:39.456 --> 00:15:40.915
I’m sure he's very upset with himself,

199
00:15:40.999 --> 00:15:44.460
and I doubt he'll listen to anyone
but you right now.

200
00:15:44.544 --> 00:15:45.753
Edward.

201
00:15:57.224 --> 00:16:00.726
l never wanted to have a party.
.  It’s not your fault.

202
00:16:02.771 --> 00:16:06.899
Jasper hasn't been away from human blood
as long as the rest of us.

203
00:16:07.651 --> 00:16:09.276
How do you do it?

204
00:16:10.237 --> 00:16:12.405
Years and years of practice.

205
00:16:12.906 --> 00:16:16.784
Did you ever think
of just doing it the easy way?

206
00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:19.704
No.

207
00:16:20.872 --> 00:16:24.291
I knew who I wanted to be.
I wanted to help people.

208
00:16:25.502 --> 00:16:28.796
It brings me happiness,
even if l am damned regardless.

209
00:16:31.299 --> 00:16:32.633
Damned?

210
00:16:33.593 --> 00:16:36.345
Like hell?

211
00:16:42.769 --> 00:16:45.229
Carlisle, you couldn't be damned.

212
00:16:45.605 --> 00:16:47.898
You couldn't. It’s impossible.

213
00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.026
Thank you, Bella.

214
00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:54.238
You've always been very gracious about us.

215
00:16:58.285 --> 00:17:01.579
So that's it?
That's why he won't change me?

216
00:17:04.624 --> 00:17:07.043
Imagine the situation in reverse. Hmm.

217
00:17:09.129 --> 00:17:11.547
If you believed as Edward does,

218
00:17:12.924 --> 00:17:15.134
could you take away his soul?

219
00:17:38.325 --> 00:17:40.201
You can't protect me

220
00:17:42.329 --> 00:17:43.996
from everything.

221
00:17:44.456 --> 00:17:47.416
At some point,
something's gonna separate us.

222
00:17:49.127 --> 00:17:51.754
It’s gonna be an accident or illness

223
00:17:52.923 --> 00:17:54.340
or old age,

224
00:17:56.093 --> 00:18:00.471
as long as I’m human.
And the only solution is to change me.

225
00:18:02.974 --> 00:18:05.684
That's not a solution. That's a tragedy.

226
00:18:05.769 --> 00:18:09.396
You're not gonna want me
when I look like a grandmother.

227
00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:22.910
Bella, do you not understand
my feelings for you at all?

228
00:18:25.664 --> 00:18:27.414
Carlisle told me

229
00:18:30.544 --> 00:18:32.670
how you feel about your soul.

230
00:18:34.256 --> 00:18:36.048
I don't believe that.

231
00:18:37.259 --> 00:18:39.385
So don't worry about mine.

232
00:18:40.512 --> 00:18:42.346
You should go inside.

233
00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:58.988
It’s still my birthday.

234
00:19:02.617 --> 00:19:04.618
So can I ask one thing?

235
00:19:08.206 --> 00:19:09.415
Kiss me?

236
00:19:40.864 --> 00:19:46.243
I love you.

237
00:20:15.148 --> 00:20:17.358
Up with your turret

238
00:20:19.653 --> 00:20:23.614
Aren't we just terrified?

239
00:20:35.293 --> 00:20:38.796
Shale, screen your worry

240
00:20:39.839 --> 00:20:43.842
From what you won't ever find

241
00:20:53.228 --> 00:21:01.527
Don't let it fool you

242
00:21:02.195 --> 00:21:04.238
Down

243
00:21:08.159 --> 00:21:09.368
Hey.

244
00:21:13.248 --> 00:21:15.708
Just come take a walk with me.

245
00:21:39.482 --> 00:21:41.400
We have to leave Forks.

246
00:21:44.696 --> 00:21:45.904
Why?

247
00:21:49.534 --> 00:21:52.995
Carlisle's supposed to be 1 0 years older
than he looks,

248
00:21:53.079 --> 00:21:55.456
and people are starting to notice.

249
00:21:58.168 --> 00:22:02.129
Okay, I’ve gotta think of something to say
to Charlie.

250
00:22:14.017 --> 00:22:15.809
When you say "we"...

251
00:22:20.106 --> 00:22:22.316
I mean my family and myself.

252
00:22:26.488 --> 00:22:30.074
Edward, what happened with Jasper,
it's nothing.

253
00:22:30.408 --> 00:22:33.118
You're right. It was nothing,

254
00:22:35.705 --> 00:22:38.248
nothing but what l always expected

255
00:22:40.251 --> 00:22:43.462
and nothing compared
to what could have happened.

256
00:22:49.469 --> 00:22:52.304
You just don't belong in my world, Bella.

257
00:22:57.352 --> 00:22:59.061
I belong with you.

258
00:23:00.814 --> 00:23:03.148
No. You don't.

259
00:23:05.652 --> 00:23:07.111
I’m coming.

260
00:23:08.154 --> 00:23:09.321
Bella,

261
00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:13.075
I don't want you to come.

262
00:23:20.625 --> 00:23:22.376
You don't want me?

263
00:23:28.133 --> 00:23:29.258
No.

264
00:23:32.929 --> 00:23:36.348
That changes things a lot.

265
00:23:37.851 --> 00:23:40.310
But if it's not too much to ask,

266
00:23:42.105 --> 00:23:44.523
can you just promise me something?

267
00:23:46.943 --> 00:23:49.111
Don't do anything reckless.

268
00:23:51.865 --> 00:23:53.657
For Charlie's sake.

269
00:23:55.076 --> 00:23:58.036
And I’ll promise something to you in return.

270
00:23:58.121 --> 00:24:00.956
This is the last time you'll ever see me.

271
00:24:01.541 --> 00:24:03.167
I won't come back,

272
00:24:03.501 --> 00:24:07.546
and you can go on with your life
without any interference from me.

273
00:24:08.339 --> 00:24:12.134
It will be like l never existed, I promise.

274
00:24:15.555 --> 00:24:19.308
lf this is about my soul, take it.
l don't want it without you.

275
00:24:19.392 --> 00:24:21.435
It’s not about your soul.

276
00:24:24.564 --> 00:24:26.899
You're just not good for me.

277
00:24:28.485 --> 00:24:30.444
Not good enough for you.

278
00:24:31.696 --> 00:24:34.323
I’m just sorry l let this go on for so long.

279
00:24:36.201 --> 00:24:37.534
Please...

280
00:24:39.078 --> 00:24:40.370
Don't...

281
00:24:45.710 --> 00:24:47.002
Goodbye.

282
00:25:02.644 --> 00:25:23.455
Edward.

283
00:25:26.459 --> 00:25:27.793
Edward!

284
00:25:35.760 --> 00:25:36.969
Edward.

285
00:27:32.585 --> 00:27:35.295
I’m gonna try the Cullens' place again.

286
00:27:36.005 --> 00:27:39.091
- The Cullens left town, Charlie.
-Good riddance.

287
00:27:39.175 --> 00:27:40.884
Where'd they go?

288
00:27:41.886 --> 00:27:43.762
We'll find her, Charlie.

289
00:27:43.846 --> 00:27:46.181
-Thanks, Harry.
-Charlie!

290
00:27:46.432 --> 00:27:47.557
Hey.

291
00:27:50.812 --> 00:27:52.437
She's all right.

292
00:27:53.272 --> 00:27:56.775
I got her. Thank you, Sam.

293
00:28:38.234 --> 00:28:51.538
There's a possibility

294
00:28:54.417 --> 00:28:58.003
All that I had

295
00:28:58.087 --> 00:29:01.673
Was all I’m gonna get

296
00:29:06.679 --> 00:29:10.015
Alice, you've disappeared,

297
00:29:12.643 --> 00:29:14.603
like everything else.

298
00:29:15.855 --> 00:29:18.565
Now who else can I talk to? I’m lost.

299
00:29:25.656 --> 00:29:27.282
When you left,

300
00:29:29.202 --> 00:29:30.869
and he left,

301
00:29:33.080 --> 00:29:35.457
you took everything with you.

302
00:29:37.543 --> 00:29:40.587
But the absence of him is everywhere I look.

303
00:29:47.970 --> 00:29:51.473
It’s like a huge hole has been punched
through my chest.

304
00:29:57.104 --> 00:29:58.230
Bella.

305
00:30:14.413 --> 00:30:16.373
But in a way I’m glad.

306
00:30:16.999 --> 00:30:20.001
The pain is my only reminder
that he was real,

307
00:30:20.211 --> 00:30:21.753
that you all were.

308
00:30:30.555 --> 00:30:32.681
All right. That's it.

309
00:30:35.434 --> 00:30:36.560
What?

310
00:30:36.978 --> 00:30:40.272
You're going to Jacksonville
to live with your mother.

311
00:30:42.608 --> 00:30:44.568
I’m not leaving Forks.

312
00:30:45.945 --> 00:30:49.739
Bells, he's not coming back.

313
00:30:52.827 --> 00:30:54.077
I know.

314
00:30:55.288 --> 00:30:58.123
It’s just not normal, this behavior.

315
00:30:58.791 --> 00:31:02.627
Quite frankly, it's scaring the hell out of me
and your mother.

316
00:31:04.297 --> 00:31:06.631
Baby, I don't want you to leave.

317
00:31:06.966 --> 00:31:11.720
I don't, but just go. Go to Jacksonville.
Make some new friends.

318
00:31:11.804 --> 00:31:13.471
I like my old friends.

319
00:31:13.556 --> 00:31:16.308
-Well, you never see them anymore.
-I do.

320
00:31:19.020 --> 00:31:24.065
I’m gonna go shopping tomorrow
with Jessica.

321
00:31:25.943 --> 00:31:28.069
-You hate shopping.
-I...

322
00:31:29.822 --> 00:31:31.948
I need a girls' night out.

323
00:31:34.785 --> 00:31:37.579
All right. Girls' night.

324
00:31:38.998 --> 00:31:40.332
Shopping.

325
00:31:41.125 --> 00:31:44.836
I like it. Go buy some stuff.

326
00:31:53.179 --> 00:31:55.180
Hi, Jessica, it's Bella.

327
00:31:56.432 --> 00:31:58.308
Yeah, Bella Swan.

328
00:32:03.356 --> 00:32:04.773
I don't know why you want to
sit through

329
00:32:04.857 --> 00:32:08.109
all those zombies eating people
and no hot guys kissing anybody.

330
00:32:08.194 --> 00:32:11.738
It’s gross. Like... And why are there
that many zombie movies anyway?

331
00:32:11.822 --> 00:32:14.407
'Cause if it's supposed to, like,
draw a parallel about leprosy,

332
00:32:14.492 --> 00:32:17.452
my cousin had leprosy.
It’s not funny, you know?

333
00:32:17.536 --> 00:32:20.455
And, like, is it supposed to be
a metaphor for consumerism?

334
00:32:20.539 --> 00:32:22.707
Because don't be so pleased
with your own, like,

335
00:32:22.792 --> 00:32:25.418
self-referential cleverness, you know?

336
00:32:25.503 --> 00:32:28.964
Like, some girls like to shop.
Not all girls, apparently.

337
00:32:29.048 --> 00:32:32.050
Although I was surprised
you even called at all. You know?

338
00:32:32.134 --> 00:32:35.261
Like, your depression thing,
I get it. I’m totally, totally worried.

339
00:32:35.346 --> 00:32:36.346
But after a while it's like,

340
00:32:36.430 --> 00:32:37.931
-you're still bumming...
- You want a ride, girls?

341
00:32:38.015 --> 00:32:39.975
...and I’m going through stuff, too.
You know? Like Mike deciding

342
00:32:40.059 --> 00:32:41.142
he just wants to be friends.

343
00:32:41.227 --> 00:32:42.185
What's up? Look what we found.

344
00:32:42.269 --> 00:32:43.478
It’s hard, you know?

345
00:32:43.562 --> 00:32:44.854
Like, and since when does "just friends"...

346
00:32:44.939 --> 00:32:46.481
1 : What's up guys?
2: Look what we found.

347
00:32:46.565 --> 00:32:48.608
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Hey, where you going?

348
00:32:56.701 --> 00:32:57.659
Keep walking.

349
00:32:59.787 --> 00:33:01.454
This is dangerous.

350
00:33:10.881 --> 00:33:13.591
-Dude, come on.
- Come here for a sec!

351
00:33:17.680 --> 00:33:19.764
I think I know those guys.

352
00:33:20.599 --> 00:33:22.684
We got beer! We got bikes!

353
00:33:23.352 --> 00:33:25.854
Well, they seem great. Can we go?

354
00:33:26.772 --> 00:33:29.107
I’m just gonna see something.

355
00:33:30.192 --> 00:33:31.609
Hey, girlie!

356
00:33:36.032 --> 00:33:38.742
All right, all right. We got a taker.

357
00:33:39.452 --> 00:33:40.869
Turn around.

358
00:33:55.634 --> 00:33:57.927
2: Shut up!
3: You shut up!

359
00:34:04.268 --> 00:34:05.435
I’m sorry, I thought you
were somebody else.

360
00:34:05.519 --> 00:34:08.354
No, that's cool.
I’ll be whoever you want me to be, honey.

361
00:34:08.439 --> 00:34:11.107
So, what do you say?

362
00:34:15.654 --> 00:34:18.239
You promised me, nothing reckless.

363
00:34:22.161 --> 00:34:25.413
You promised it would be
as if you never existed.

364
00:34:30.920 --> 00:34:33.671
-You lied.
-You say something, babe?

365
00:34:33.756 --> 00:34:35.256
You know what? Never mind.

366
00:34:52.399 --> 00:34:55.026
Stop! Stop, stop, stop!

367
00:35:05.037 --> 00:35:07.956
Hey, what the hell's wrong with you?

368
00:35:08.040 --> 00:35:09.707
Just curious.

369
00:35:11.210 --> 00:35:14.129
-l thought that l saw something.
-You... Oh.

370
00:35:14.547 --> 00:35:17.841
You're insane, actually. Or suicidal.

371
00:35:18.342 --> 00:35:20.927
That homeboy could've been a psycho.

372
00:35:21.470 --> 00:35:25.390
I was about to end up in an
interview room like some lame  show.

373
00:35:25.683 --> 00:35:27.725
God, that was such a rush.

374
00:35:29.436 --> 00:35:31.980
Awesome.
So you're an adrenaline junkie now?

375
00:35:32.064 --> 00:35:33.314
That's cool. You can go bungee jumping.

376
00:35:33.399 --> 00:35:36.651
You don't get on the back
of some random loser's motorcycle.

377
00:35:36.735 --> 00:35:37.902
Crazy.

378
00:35:42.408 --> 00:35:45.076
Alice, I saw him.

379
00:35:47.163 --> 00:35:49.998
Maybe I’m crazy now. I guess that's okay.

380
00:35:52.126 --> 00:35:55.378
If a rush of danger
is what it takes to see him,

381
00:35:55.462 --> 00:35:57.714
then that's what I’ll find.

382
00:36:01.802 --> 00:36:02.969
Bella!

383
00:36:04.054 --> 00:36:06.139
Where the hell have you been, loca?

384
00:36:10.186 --> 00:36:12.645
I brought you something.

385
00:36:13.314 --> 00:36:15.940
-Okay.
-It’s a little crazy.

386
00:36:20.988 --> 00:36:22.071
Wow.

387
00:36:22.448 --> 00:36:24.657
Scrap metal. You shouldn't have.

388
00:36:24.742 --> 00:36:26.951
I saved it from the junkyard.

389
00:36:29.205 --> 00:36:33.082
I think they'll probably cost more to fix
than they're worth,

390
00:36:33.334 --> 00:36:35.585
but then I thought that
if l had a mechanic friend

391
00:36:35.669 --> 00:36:36.920
-to help me out then...
-Ah!

392
00:36:37.004 --> 00:36:40.381
-Me being the mechanic-type friend?
-That's right.

393
00:36:41.550 --> 00:36:44.594
-Since when are you into motorcycles?
-Since now.

394
00:36:49.975 --> 00:36:53.853
I get it if you think that
this is really stupid and reckless.

395
00:36:53.938 --> 00:36:56.981
Yeah, I mean,
it's completely stupid and reckless.

396
00:36:59.985 --> 00:37:01.611
When do we start?

397
00:37:03.864 --> 00:37:04.864
Um.

398
00:37:05.699 --> 00:37:06.991
Now.

399
00:37:07.826 --> 00:37:09.661
-Please?
- All right.

400
00:37:12.122 --> 00:37:16.459
Oh, hey, be careful.
Those things are actually really heavy, so...

401
00:37:21.799 --> 00:37:24.050
Jake, you're, like, buff.

402
00:37:24.134 --> 00:37:26.386
How did that happen?
You're, like, 16. I don't get it.

403
00:37:26.470 --> 00:37:29.806
Mmm-hmm. Age is just a number, baby.
What are you, like, 40 now?

404
00:37:34.144 --> 00:37:36.437
It feels like that sometimes.

405
00:37:46.657 --> 00:37:49.367
That song's good. You don't like it?

406
00:37:50.494 --> 00:37:54.872
I don't really like music anymore, kind of.

407
00:37:55.541 --> 00:37:58.042
Okay. No more music.

408
00:38:01.213 --> 00:38:03.298
So I was thinking,
if we're gonna do this every day,

409
00:38:03.382 --> 00:38:05.216
and hopefully we will,

410
00:38:05.301 --> 00:38:08.011
we have to, like,
fit some homework in there somewhere.

411
00:38:08.095 --> 00:38:11.139
I don't want Billy thinking that
I’m a bad influence on you.

412
00:38:11.223 --> 00:38:14.350
You? Influence me? Please.

413
00:38:16.729 --> 00:38:19.230
Are you... I’m older than you,

414
00:38:19.315 --> 00:38:22.650
so that makes me the influencer
and you the influence.

415
00:38:22.735 --> 00:38:24.319
No, no, no.

416
00:38:24.403 --> 00:38:28.156
My size and knowledge base
actually makes me older than you

417
00:38:28.240 --> 00:38:30.742
because of your general paleness
and lack of know-how.

418
00:38:30.826 --> 00:38:33.328
I convinced you to build
two-wheeled death machines with me.

419
00:38:33.412 --> 00:38:36.956
Don't you think that makes you
kind of young and naive?

420
00:38:37.041 --> 00:38:39.250
Okay. So where do we stand?

421
00:38:40.252 --> 00:38:43.212
-I’m 35. And you might be, like, 32.
-Come on.

422
00:38:44.423 --> 00:38:48.009
- Yo, Jake, you in there?
-It’s okay. It’s just my boys.

423
00:38:48.093 --> 00:38:50.845
-Hey, Jake.
-Hey. Guys, this is Bella.

424
00:38:50.929 --> 00:38:53.473
-Bella, that's Quil and Embry.
-Hi.

425
00:38:54.141 --> 00:38:55.933
I’m Quil Ateara.

426
00:38:58.020 --> 00:38:59.937
So the bike building story is true.

427
00:39:00.022 --> 00:39:02.106
Oh, yeah, yeah,
I taught him everything he knows.

428
00:39:02.191 --> 00:39:04.984
What about the part
where you're his girlfriend?

429
00:39:05.611 --> 00:39:06.611
Uh...

430
00:39:06.695 --> 00:39:08.529
We're friends, you know.

431
00:39:08.614 --> 00:39:10.239
- Burn.
-Actually,

432
00:39:10.324 --> 00:39:13.201
remember I said she's a girl and a friend.

433
00:39:13.285 --> 00:39:15.161
Embry, do you remember him
making that distinction?

434
00:39:15.245 --> 00:39:16.204
Nope.

435
00:39:16.288 --> 00:39:18.790
So you guys have girlfriends?
That's awesome.

436
00:39:20.042 --> 00:39:23.586
Yeah, right.
Quil's actually taking his cousin to prom.

437
00:39:24.213 --> 00:39:25.380
Yeah, that's still a riot.

438
00:39:25.464 --> 00:39:28.424
You want funny, Black? I’ll give you funny.

439
00:39:29.760 --> 00:39:31.052
Jeez.

440
00:39:31.136 --> 00:39:32.470
Hey, that hold's illegal!

441
00:39:32.554 --> 00:39:34.555
I got five bucks on Quil.

442
00:39:34.890 --> 00:39:36.265
You're on.

443
00:39:38.310 --> 00:39:42.772
All of the astronauts
Champagne in plastic cups

444
00:39:42.856 --> 00:39:47.151
Waiting for the big hero to show

445
00:39:47.319 --> 00:39:52.323
Outside the door he stands
His head in his hands

446
00:39:52.491 --> 00:39:55.576
And his heart in his throat

447
00:39:55.661 --> 00:39:58.704
What can he tell them now

448
00:39:59.039 --> 00:40:00.289
Dear Alice,

449
00:40:00.374 --> 00:40:02.750
I wish I had your real address.

450
00:40:03.168 --> 00:40:05.753
I wish I could tell you about Jake.

451
00:40:06.004 --> 00:40:08.214
He makes me feel better.

452
00:40:09.383 --> 00:40:11.843
I mean, he makes me feel alive.

453
00:40:14.388 --> 00:40:16.514
The hole in my chest,

454
00:40:17.182 --> 00:40:21.644
well, when I’m with Jake,
it's like it's almost healed

455
00:40:22.771 --> 00:40:24.105
for a while.

456
00:40:24.356 --> 00:40:28.693
So, Quil keeps asking to come over.
I think he likes you a little too much.

457
00:40:29.194 --> 00:40:30.194
Oh.

458
00:40:31.071 --> 00:40:34.866
Well, I’m really not into
the whole cougar thing. You know?

459
00:40:37.035 --> 00:40:39.036
What's up with you and age?

460
00:40:39.538 --> 00:40:42.498
I mean,
how old was that Cullen guy, anyway?

461
00:40:45.085 --> 00:40:47.962
But even Jake can't keep
the dreams away.

462
00:40:56.680 --> 00:40:58.347
Hey, hey, hey!

463
00:40:59.057 --> 00:41:00.224
Wake up, Bella.

464
00:41:00.309 --> 00:41:02.977
You're okay. You're okay.

465
00:41:14.072 --> 00:41:18.493
I thought this thing was starting to work,
but I guess not.

466
00:41:24.875 --> 00:41:26.918
Can I ask you something?

467
00:41:28.921 --> 00:41:30.838
Hanging out with Jacob,

468
00:41:31.757 --> 00:41:35.468
that seems to take your mind
off things a bit, doesn't it?

469
00:41:40.516 --> 00:41:42.266
You know, sometimes

470
00:41:44.186 --> 00:41:47.313
you gotta learn to love what's good for you.

471
00:41:48.232 --> 00:41:50.066
You know what I mean?

472
00:41:52.569 --> 00:41:54.612
Of course, what do I know?

473
00:41:54.988 --> 00:41:57.281
I’m just a terminal bachelor.

474
00:41:59.576 --> 00:42:01.577
Famous ladies' man.

475
00:42:04.122 --> 00:42:05.248
Okay.

476
00:42:07.125 --> 00:42:08.751
I’m gonna go to bed.

477
00:42:09.461 --> 00:42:10.461
Uh...

478
00:42:10.963 --> 00:42:12.380
I love you.

479
00:42:18.512 --> 00:42:23.057
lf l told you l couldn't have fixed
these bikes, what would you have said?

480
00:42:25.477 --> 00:42:27.895
Are you doubting your mad skills?

481
00:42:28.564 --> 00:42:31.941
No. Definitely not. I mean, they'll run fine.

482
00:42:32.859 --> 00:42:34.318
It’s just,

483
00:42:36.196 --> 00:42:40.032
maybe if I was smart,
I would have dragged out the rebuild a bit.

484
00:42:44.162 --> 00:42:49.166
If you told me you couldn't fix these bikes,
I would say that that's really too bad,

485
00:42:49.251 --> 00:42:53.129
but that we're just gonna
have to find something else to do.

486
00:42:58.302 --> 00:43:00.011
Is that Sam Uley?

487
00:43:01.013 --> 00:43:03.389
Yeah. Him and his cult.

488
00:43:06.268 --> 00:43:07.727
Oh, my God.

489
00:43:10.814 --> 00:43:12.523
Did you see that?

490
00:43:18.280 --> 00:43:22.116
They're not really fighting, Bella.
They're cliff diving.

491
00:43:22.200 --> 00:43:24.702
Scary as hell, but a total rush.

492
00:43:27.998 --> 00:43:30.791
-A rush?
-Most of us jump from lower down.

493
00:43:30.876 --> 00:43:34.211
We leave the showing off
to Sam and his disciples.

494
00:43:36.423 --> 00:43:39.717
You have some kind of beef with him
or something?

495
00:43:40.886 --> 00:43:42.386
l don't know.

496
00:43:42.471 --> 00:43:45.056
They just think they run this place.

497
00:43:45.474 --> 00:43:48.351
Embry used to call them
hall monitors on steroids.

498
00:43:48.435 --> 00:43:50.895
-Now look at him.
-That's Embry?

499
00:43:52.731 --> 00:43:55.066
-Yeah.
-What happened to him?

500
00:43:55.567 --> 00:43:57.109
He missed some school.

501
00:43:57.194 --> 00:44:01.280
Now all of a sudden, he started
following Sam around like a little puppy.

502
00:44:01.365 --> 00:44:04.200
Same thing happened with Paul and Jared.

503
00:44:04.660 --> 00:44:06.952
Sam keeps giving me this look,

504
00:44:09.039 --> 00:44:11.749
like he's waiting for me or something.

505
00:44:13.043 --> 00:44:15.753
It’s kind of starting to freak me out.

506
00:44:15.837 --> 00:44:18.255
Well, you should just avoid him.

507
00:44:20.258 --> 00:44:21.592
I try.

508
00:44:38.735 --> 00:44:40.069
Okay.

509
00:44:43.156 --> 00:44:45.282
-You look scared.
-I’m not.

510
00:44:46.743 --> 00:44:48.035
All right.

511
00:44:48.120 --> 00:44:50.121
-Brake?
-That one.

512
00:44:53.458 --> 00:44:54.834
Clutch?

513
00:44:54.918 --> 00:44:56.127
Good.

514
00:44:56.461 --> 00:44:57.586
Gas?

515
00:45:00.090 --> 00:45:01.340
Ready?

516
00:45:02.467 --> 00:45:05.553
Now, slowly release the clutch.

517
00:45:07.556 --> 00:45:08.764
Bella.

518
00:45:12.310 --> 00:45:13.310
Stop.

519
00:45:15.188 --> 00:45:16.188
Whoa!

520
00:45:18.650 --> 00:45:20.234
You all right?

521
00:45:21.528 --> 00:45:23.320
I’m gonna go again.

522
00:45:23.739 --> 00:45:24.905
Okay.

523
00:45:38.503 --> 00:45:39.503
Ah!

524
00:45:40.964 --> 00:45:41.964
Whoa!

525
00:45:43.675 --> 00:45:45.176
Hit the brake!

526
00:45:59.775 --> 00:46:00.775
I wanna go again.

527
00:46:00.859 --> 00:46:02.610
Are you trying to get yourself killed?

528
00:46:02.694 --> 00:46:05.237
-No. l want to go again.
-No. Forget it.

529
00:46:06.031 --> 00:46:07.698
No more bikes.

530
00:46:08.617 --> 00:46:10.201
Man, your head.

531
00:46:10.827 --> 00:46:11.827
Ow.

532
00:46:13.246 --> 00:46:15.498
-Yeah.
-Oh, my God, I’m sorry.

533
00:46:16.708 --> 00:46:19.376
What, you're apologizing for bleeding?

534
00:46:21.546 --> 00:46:23.339
Yeah. I guess I am.

535
00:46:24.216 --> 00:46:27.092
Well, it's just blood, Bella. No big deal.

536
00:46:32.390 --> 00:46:33.641
There.

537
00:46:40.232 --> 00:46:42.274
What are you staring at?

538
00:46:45.654 --> 00:46:47.780
You're sort of beautiful.

539
00:46:55.664 --> 00:46:57.998
How hard did you hit your head?

540
00:46:59.459 --> 00:47:00.501
I don't know.

541
00:47:02.879 --> 00:47:04.255
Let's go.

542
00:47:07.717 --> 00:47:09.176
I did see something in the woods.

543
00:47:09.719 --> 00:47:11.095
Totally. Baby, l believe you.

544
00:47:11.179 --> 00:47:13.472
No, he doesn't. He's just trying to get lucky.

545
00:47:14.891 --> 00:47:18.894
No, okay. It was jet black and huge.

546
00:47:18.979 --> 00:47:21.814
On all fours, it was still taller than a person.

547
00:47:21.898 --> 00:47:23.065
A bear, maybe?

548
00:47:23.149 --> 00:47:25.609
Or an alien.
You're lucky you didn't get probed.

549
00:47:27.028 --> 00:47:29.029
Well, I saw it.

550
00:47:29.781 --> 00:47:31.782
You know, you're not the only one.

551
00:47:32.617 --> 00:47:35.244
My dad's been getting reports at the station.

552
00:47:35.328 --> 00:47:38.247
Like, five hikers have been killed
by some bear.

553
00:47:38.331 --> 00:47:40.457
But they can't find the bear.

554
00:47:40.542 --> 00:47:41.542
Hmm.

555
00:47:43.628 --> 00:47:46.505
Last time you clowns doubt my girlfriend.

556
00:47:47.257 --> 00:47:48.215
Um...

557
00:47:50.635 --> 00:47:52.094
So? I mean,

558
00:47:52.929 --> 00:47:54.555
Bella's back?

559
00:47:58.351 --> 00:47:59.935
Yeah, I guess so.

560
00:48:00.020 --> 00:48:02.605
All right, that's... Well, welcome.

561
00:48:03.607 --> 00:48:06.692
So, listen, now that you're talking

562
00:48:08.236 --> 00:48:12.865
and eating again, which, you know,
you've got to get that protein in there,

563
00:48:14.993 --> 00:48:19.204
I was just wondering if you wanted to go
see a movie with me.

564
00:48:23.251 --> 00:48:25.878
Yeah. Sure. Yeah, l do.

565
00:48:27.756 --> 00:48:29.006
Cool.

566
00:48:29.090 --> 00:48:31.592
Let me see, we could check out

567
00:48:32.177 --> 00:48:34.428
Love Spelled Backwards Is Love.

568
00:48:34.512 --> 00:48:37.598
You know, it's a dumb title,
but it's a romantic comedy.

569
00:48:37.682 --> 00:48:40.517
-I mean, it's supposed to be pretty...
-No. No romance.

570
00:48:44.606 --> 00:48:47.691
How about Face Punch?
Have you heard of that?

571
00:48:48.526 --> 00:48:50.945
I mean, that's an action movie.

572
00:48:51.029 --> 00:48:52.863
Yeah, that's perfect.

573
00:48:53.698 --> 00:48:55.532
Guns, adrenaline.

574
00:48:56.368 --> 00:48:57.618
That's my thing.

575
00:48:57.702 --> 00:48:58.869
Okay.

576
00:48:59.204 --> 00:49:03.540
We should get a bunch of people to go.
Do you guys want to go see Face Punch?

577
00:49:03.625 --> 00:49:04.833
Face Punch, yeah!

578
00:49:04.918 --> 00:49:06.418
Mike, hey,
we were supposed to watch that.

579
00:49:06.503 --> 00:49:08.045
Remember, the trailer's like...

580
00:49:08.129 --> 00:49:10.339
-"Punch faces."
-I remember.

581
00:49:10.423 --> 00:49:13.133
Yeah!
Movie night with Bella.

582
00:49:16.388 --> 00:49:18.222
So Face Punch, huh?

583
00:49:18.890 --> 00:49:20.891
You like action movies?

584
00:49:21.810 --> 00:49:23.310
Not really.

585
00:49:26.272 --> 00:49:29.066
I heard it sucks. Bad.

586
00:49:30.568 --> 00:49:33.445
Are you even old enough to see this movie?

587
00:49:34.406 --> 00:49:36.156
I mean, you know, without,
like, adult supervision.

588
00:49:36.241 --> 00:49:38.158
Right, yeah, well,
she's buying my ticket for me.

589
00:49:38.243 --> 00:49:40.202
She's buying it. Okay.

590
00:49:41.287 --> 00:49:44.248
Jessica bailed,
and Angela got the stomach flu,

591
00:49:44.332 --> 00:49:46.583
so Eric's taking care of her.

592
00:49:47.585 --> 00:49:49.753
-It’s just us three.
-Great!

593
00:49:50.839 --> 00:49:52.381
-Great.
-Yeah.

594
00:49:55.552 --> 00:49:56.844
1   Put your gun down.

595
00:49:56.928 --> 00:49:59.638
2   Put your gun down
or I’m gonna blow your frickin' head off.

596
00:49:59.723 --> 00:50:02.182
3   Both of you put both
of your guns down

597
00:50:02.267 --> 00:50:04.977
or I’m gonna blow both
of your frickin' heads off.

598
00:50:06.396 --> 00:50:07.855
1   All right, forget it,
let's do this!

599
00:50:26.291 --> 00:50:28.792
Okay, I think I’m gonna throw up.

600
00:50:35.008 --> 00:50:36.300
He's...

601
00:50:36.676 --> 00:50:38.469
What a marshmallow!

602
00:50:39.637 --> 00:50:43.057
You should hold out for someone
with a stronger stomach.

603
00:50:43.141 --> 00:50:46.602
Someone who laughs at the gore
that makes weaker men vomit.

604
00:50:46.686 --> 00:50:48.520
Yeah. I’ll keep my eye open for that.

605
00:50:50.815 --> 00:50:55.152
I feel bad. He probably has
that flu that's going around.

606
00:50:58.490 --> 00:51:00.824
What? I can't hold your hand?

607
00:51:00.909 --> 00:51:02.951
No, of course you can.

608
00:51:05.789 --> 00:51:09.833
I just think it means, you know,
something a little different to you. So...

609
00:51:12.003 --> 00:51:15.422
Okay, well, tell me something.
You like me, right?

610
00:51:20.261 --> 00:51:22.930
And you think I’m sort of beautiful?

611
00:51:24.015 --> 00:51:27.643
Jacob, please, don't do this.

612
00:51:34.400 --> 00:51:35.526
Why?

613
00:51:38.947 --> 00:51:41.740
Because you're about to ruin everything.

614
00:51:43.576 --> 00:51:46.203
And I need you.

615
00:51:53.128 --> 00:51:55.587
Well, I’ve got loads of time.

616
00:51:56.714 --> 00:51:58.632
I’m not gonna give up.

617
00:51:59.759 --> 00:52:02.386
I don't want you to,

618
00:52:04.639 --> 00:52:07.850
but it's just 'cause I don't want you
to go anywhere.

619
00:52:10.395 --> 00:52:12.646
And that's really selfish.

620
00:52:16.151 --> 00:52:19.403
You know,
I’m not like a car that you can fix up.

621
00:52:23.533 --> 00:52:27.578
I’m never gonna run right.
So I should be fair to you.

622
00:52:29.998 --> 00:52:32.249
It’s because of him, right?

623
00:52:42.552 --> 00:52:43.760
Look,

624
00:52:45.430 --> 00:52:47.848
I know what he did to you.

625
00:52:49.225 --> 00:52:53.437
But, Bella, l would never ever do that.

626
00:52:56.149 --> 00:52:59.359
I won't ever hurt you. l promise.

627
00:53:00.862 --> 00:53:02.779
I won't let you down.

628
00:53:03.740 --> 00:53:05.616
You can count on me.

629
00:53:13.458 --> 00:53:14.458
Well,

630
00:53:19.881 --> 00:53:21.632
I need to go home.

631
00:53:28.765 --> 00:53:31.642
I was feeling sick before the movie. Okay?

632
00:53:34.854 --> 00:53:36.188
What is your problem?

633
00:53:36.272 --> 00:53:38.523
Right now? You're my problem.

634
00:53:39.192 --> 00:53:42.527
Feeling sick?
Maybe you need to go to the hospital.

635
00:53:43.655 --> 00:53:45.489
You want me to put you in the hospital?

636
00:53:45.573 --> 00:53:48.909
Jake! Jake. Jake, the movie's over.
What are you doing?

637
00:53:49.327 --> 00:53:51.954
You're really hot.

638
00:53:53.498 --> 00:53:56.792
Like, you feel like you have a fever.
Are you okay?

639
00:53:57.794 --> 00:54:00.087
I don't know what's happening.

640
00:54:02.048 --> 00:54:03.548
I gotta go.

641
00:54:08.638 --> 00:54:10.347
That dude is weird.

642
00:54:13.851 --> 00:54:16.520
Jake,
your dad says you have mono.

643
00:54:17.105 --> 00:54:20.274
He won't let me visit,
but would you call me?

644
00:54:25.822 --> 00:54:28.448
Hey, it's me again. I just...

645
00:54:29.492 --> 00:54:32.411
I’m sorry about what I said
at the movie theater.

646
00:54:33.496 --> 00:54:36.707
I just wanted to hear your voice,
so no pressure.

647
00:54:39.836 --> 00:54:41.253
Jacob, please...

648
00:54:43.214 --> 00:54:44.589
Call me.

649
00:54:44.674 --> 00:54:47.301
Okay. We should be back around 3:00.

650
00:54:54.350 --> 00:54:55.517
Hey.

651
00:54:56.436 --> 00:54:58.437
Look, l don't have to go fishing today.

652
00:54:58.521 --> 00:54:59.938
Yes, you do.

653
00:55:00.315 --> 00:55:02.941
Yeah, you do.
Go. What are you talking about?

654
00:55:03.026 --> 00:55:04.693
Just be careful.

655
00:55:04.777 --> 00:55:06.236
Always am.

656
00:55:07.905 --> 00:55:10.407
Those bears won't get the drop on me,
Bella.

657
00:55:10.491 --> 00:55:12.492
My kung fu is strong.

658
00:55:45.735 --> 00:55:46.902
Jake!

659
00:55:47.904 --> 00:55:49.154
Hey!

660
00:55:53.993 --> 00:55:55.952
You cut your hair off?

661
00:55:58.790 --> 00:56:00.624
And got a tattoo?

662
00:56:03.961 --> 00:56:05.170
Bella.

663
00:56:05.254 --> 00:56:08.215
l thought you were too sick to come outside

664
00:56:09.133 --> 00:56:11.843
or pick up the phone when l call.

665
00:56:13.096 --> 00:56:14.429
Go away.

666
00:56:15.765 --> 00:56:16.932
What?

667
00:56:18.601 --> 00:56:19.935
Go away.

668
00:56:21.896 --> 00:56:24.064
What happened to you? What's...

669
00:56:24.148 --> 00:56:26.441
Hey! What happened?

670
00:56:29.404 --> 00:56:32.447
Did Sam get to you?
Is that what's happening?

671
00:56:32.532 --> 00:56:35.826
Sam's trying to help me. Don't blame him.

672
00:56:36.953 --> 00:56:39.413
But if you want somebody to blame,

673
00:56:39.580 --> 00:56:43.500
how about those filthy bloodsuckers
you love, the Cullens?

674
00:56:50.716 --> 00:56:51.842
l don't know what you're talking about.

675
00:56:51.926 --> 00:56:54.636
No, you know exactly
what I’m talking about.

676
00:56:54.720 --> 00:56:57.514
You've been lying to everyone. Charlie.

677
00:56:59.809 --> 00:57:01.852
But you can't lie to me.

678
00:57:02.937 --> 00:57:05.105
-Not anymore, Bella.
- Jacob!

679
00:57:05.773 --> 00:57:07.107
Jacob!

680
00:57:13.156 --> 00:57:14.656
Look, Bella,

681
00:57:15.867 --> 00:57:18.201
we can't be friends anymore.

682
00:57:19.078 --> 00:57:22.873
Look, Jake,
l know that I’ve been hurting you.

683
00:57:24.542 --> 00:57:27.544
It’s killing me. It kills me.

684
00:57:29.839 --> 00:57:32.632
l just need... Maybe give me, like,

685
00:57:32.717 --> 00:57:34.718
-some time or something.
-Look, don't.

686
00:57:35.678 --> 00:57:37.220
It’s not you.

687
00:57:40.099 --> 00:57:43.018
It’s not you, it's me, right? Really?

688
00:57:43.936 --> 00:57:46.271
It’s true. It is me.

689
00:57:49.233 --> 00:57:51.359
I’m not good.

690
00:57:54.155 --> 00:57:57.365
l used to be a good kid.

691
00:57:58.701 --> 00:58:00.076
Not anymore.

692
00:58:01.245 --> 00:58:03.872
This doesn't even matter. All right?

693
00:58:04.165 --> 00:58:05.165
This is over.

694
00:58:05.249 --> 00:58:07.417
You can't break up with me.

695
00:58:09.337 --> 00:58:10.587
l mean...

696
00:58:12.006 --> 00:58:14.257
l mean, you're my best friend.

697
00:58:16.761 --> 00:58:18.512
You promised me.

698
00:58:19.972 --> 00:58:21.306
l know.

699
00:58:22.141 --> 00:58:24.893
l promised l wouldn't hurt you, Bella.

700
00:58:25.728 --> 00:58:28.271
And this is me keeping that promise.

701
00:58:29.065 --> 00:58:30.398
Go home

702
00:58:31.108 --> 00:58:34.569
and don't come back
or you're gonna get hurt.

703
00:58:48.084 --> 00:58:49.417
Alice,

704
00:58:50.461 --> 00:58:51.962
things are...

705
00:58:53.589 --> 00:58:55.465
Things are bad again.

706
00:58:56.676 --> 00:58:59.803
Without Jake, l just... l can't stand it.

707
00:59:03.140 --> 00:59:05.433
l don't see Edward anymore.

708
00:59:06.894 --> 00:59:09.813
Will it really feel like he never existed?

709
00:59:17.321 --> 00:59:20.490
l will find the place
where l can see him again.

710
01:00:15.755 --> 01:00:16.963
Bella.

711
01:00:18.007 --> 01:00:19.257
Laurent.

712
01:00:21.260 --> 01:00:23.762
l didn't expect to find you here.

713
01:00:25.890 --> 01:00:30.226
l went to visit the Cullens,
but the house is empty.

714
01:00:32.563 --> 01:00:35.065
I’m surprised they left you behind.

715
01:00:35.274 --> 01:00:37.275
Weren't you sort of

716
01:00:38.402 --> 01:00:40.028
a pet of theirs?

717
01:00:40.988 --> 01:00:42.530
Yeah. You could say that.

718
01:00:42.615 --> 01:00:44.949
Do the Cullens visit often?

719
01:00:50.164 --> 01:00:51.164
Lie.

720
01:00:56.754 --> 01:00:58.046
Yeah, absolutely, all the time.

721
01:00:58.130 --> 01:00:59.673
Lie better.

722
01:00:59.757 --> 01:01:02.384
I’ll tell them that you stopped by.

723
01:01:02.968 --> 01:01:05.178
But l probably shouldn't

724
01:01:05.638 --> 01:01:08.306
tell Edward,

725
01:01:10.101 --> 01:01:11.476
'cause he's pretty protective.

726
01:01:11.560 --> 01:01:13.770
But he's far away, isn't he?

727
01:01:16.649 --> 01:01:18.400
Why are you here?

728
01:01:18.484 --> 01:01:22.862
I came as a favor to Victoria.

729
01:01:26.325 --> 01:01:27.867
-Victoria?
-She asked me to see

730
01:01:27.952 --> 01:01:31.538
if you were still under
the protection of the Cullens.

731
01:01:31.622 --> 01:01:35.041
Victoria feels it's only fair
to kill Edward's mate,

732
01:01:35.584 --> 01:01:37.252
given he killed hers.

733
01:01:37.336 --> 01:01:39.129
An eye for an eye.

734
01:01:39.797 --> 01:01:40.964
Threaten him.

735
01:01:41.048 --> 01:01:44.551
Edward would know who did it.
And he'd come after you.

736
01:01:45.594 --> 01:01:47.512
l don't think he will.

737
01:01:48.723 --> 01:01:51.683
After all, how much could you mean to him

738
01:01:52.143 --> 01:01:54.644
if he left you here unprotected?

739
01:01:56.981 --> 01:01:59.983
Victoria won't be happy
about my killing you,

740
01:02:00.067 --> 01:02:02.068
but l can't help myself.

741
01:02:02.361 --> 01:02:04.112
You are so mouth-watering.

742
01:02:04.196 --> 01:02:07.907
-Please, don't. l mean, you helped us.
-No, no, no, no.

743
01:02:09.118 --> 01:02:12.370
Don't be afraid. I’m doing you a kindness.

744
01:02:12.663 --> 01:02:15.331
Victoria plans on killing you
slowly,

745
01:02:16.625 --> 01:02:17.959
painfully,

746
01:02:18.919 --> 01:02:21.171
whereas I’ll make it quick.

747
01:02:21.505 --> 01:02:22.881
l promise.

748
01:02:23.883 --> 01:02:25.884
You will feel nothing.

749
01:02:31.640 --> 01:02:33.266
Edward, l love you.

750
01:02:35.644 --> 01:02:37.312
l don't believe it.

751
01:03:44.380 --> 01:03:46.923
-Dad! l saw them.
-What's the matter?

752
01:03:47.007 --> 01:03:50.009
-In the woods. They're not bears.
-What do you mean "in the woods"?

753
01:03:50.094 --> 01:03:51.845
Bell, what the hell
were you doing out in the woods?

754
01:03:51.929 --> 01:03:55.640
They're wolves.
l mean, they're like huge wolves.

755
01:03:55.724 --> 01:03:57.559
Are you sure about that, Bella?

756
01:03:57.643 --> 01:04:00.854
Yeah! l just saw them.
They were after something.

757
01:04:02.064 --> 01:04:03.273
Wolves?

758
01:04:04.441 --> 01:04:05.942
You saw them?

759
01:04:08.571 --> 01:04:11.114
All right, well, Harry,

760
01:04:12.408 --> 01:04:15.743
feel like going hunting?
Get some of your guys together?

761
01:04:16.203 --> 01:04:18.246
Sure, yeah, I’ll just...

762
01:04:19.999 --> 01:04:21.833
By now, those wolves will be dead,

763
01:04:23.460 --> 01:04:26.504
and Laurent would have told her
I’m unprotected.

764
01:04:26.589 --> 01:04:27.839
Victoria.

765
01:04:29.592 --> 01:04:31.050
l should go to the station.

766
01:04:31.135 --> 01:04:33.595
Yeah, you should. You should go.

767
01:04:34.221 --> 01:04:36.598
Can you just stay in the house?

768
01:05:01.624 --> 01:05:02.874
Bella!

769
01:05:05.544 --> 01:05:06.961
You scared me.

770
01:05:07.046 --> 01:05:10.506
-What the hell are you doing?
-Back up. I’m coming up.

771
01:05:22.770 --> 01:05:23.978
Hey.

772
01:05:26.148 --> 01:05:27.857
Look, I’m sorry.

773
01:05:34.907 --> 01:05:37.200
-For what?
-l wish l could explain.

774
01:05:37.284 --> 01:05:40.411
But l literally can't.

775
01:05:49.171 --> 01:05:52.548
Have you ever had a secret
you couldn't tell anyone,

776
01:05:53.467 --> 01:05:55.927
one that wasn't yours to share?

777
01:05:58.847 --> 01:06:01.391
Well, that's what it's like for me.

778
01:06:01.642 --> 01:06:02.976
But worse.

779
01:06:04.353 --> 01:06:07.730
You have no idea how tight I’m bound.

780
01:06:08.899 --> 01:06:10.358
l hate this.

781
01:06:11.276 --> 01:06:13.277
l hate what they've done to you.

782
01:06:27.751 --> 01:06:30.837
l mean, the killer part is, you already know.

783
01:06:34.925 --> 01:06:39.637
Bella, do you remember
when we walked on the beach at La Push?

784
01:06:41.181 --> 01:06:42.473
The...

785
01:06:46.478 --> 01:06:49.147
The story. The story about

786
01:06:50.441 --> 01:06:52.108
the cold ones.

787
01:06:53.819 --> 01:06:57.572
l guess l understand
why that's the only part you remember.

788
01:07:04.580 --> 01:07:08.416
There's gotta be something that you can do.

789
01:07:08.500 --> 01:07:10.543
No. I’m in it for life.

790
01:07:11.962 --> 01:07:14.589
Well, maybe we should just
get out of here for a while.

791
01:07:14.673 --> 01:07:16.549
Just leave,

792
01:07:16.633 --> 01:07:18.259
just you and me.

793
01:07:18.677 --> 01:07:20.303
You'd do that?

794
01:07:23.432 --> 01:07:25.391
l would do it for you.

795
01:07:31.648 --> 01:07:35.026
It’s not something
l can just run away from, Bella.

796
01:07:35.986 --> 01:07:39.489
But l would run away with you

797
01:07:43.744 --> 01:07:45.161
if l could.

798
01:07:49.291 --> 01:07:52.502
l gotta go.
They'll start wondering where l am.

799
01:07:56.673 --> 01:07:58.174
Come here.

800
01:08:02.429 --> 01:08:03.721
Please,

801
01:08:04.765 --> 01:08:06.557
try to remember.

802
01:08:08.185 --> 01:08:10.311
It'd be so much easier

803
01:08:11.522 --> 01:08:13.147
if you knew.

804
01:08:15.609 --> 01:08:18.152
I’ll try. But, Jake...

805
01:08:18.946 --> 01:08:21.697
Jake, what are you doing? Wait, Jake.

806
01:08:28.831 --> 01:08:29.997
Jake.

807
01:08:46.890 --> 01:08:48.641
Edward, I’m scared.

808
01:08:49.226 --> 01:08:50.852
You should be.

809
01:08:55.899 --> 01:08:57.817
Really, it's just like an old story.

810
01:08:57.901 --> 01:08:59.777
I’m not really supposed
to say anything about it.

811
01:08:59.862 --> 01:09:03.656
Did you know Quileutes
are supposedly descended from wolves?

812
01:09:18.505 --> 01:09:19.755
Bella?

813
01:09:20.174 --> 01:09:21.924
l need to see him.

814
01:09:22.634 --> 01:09:24.177
He's not in.

815
01:09:25.846 --> 01:09:29.140
-Okay, I’m sorry, l really need to see him.
-Bella!

816
01:09:45.115 --> 01:09:46.782
What did you do?

817
01:09:47.784 --> 01:09:48.826
-Okay, what did you do?
-Hey.

818
01:09:48.911 --> 01:09:50.286
-What did you do to him?
-Easy!

819
01:09:50.370 --> 01:09:51.412
He didn't want this.

820
01:09:51.496 --> 01:09:53.873
What did we do? What did he do?
What'd he tell you?

821
01:09:53.957 --> 01:09:55.374
-Both of you calm down.
-Nothing.

822
01:09:55.459 --> 01:09:58.544
He tells me nothing
because he's scared of you.

823
01:10:03.675 --> 01:10:05.593
-Too late now.
- Bella, get back!

824
01:10:06.803 --> 01:10:09.513
Paul, calm down, now!

825
01:10:18.148 --> 01:10:19.398
Bella!

826
01:10:20.651 --> 01:10:21.776
Run!

827
01:10:24.988 --> 01:10:26.322
Jake, run!

828
01:10:52.516 --> 01:10:53.683
Paul!

829
01:11:04.361 --> 01:11:07.029
Hey! Take Bella back to Emily's place.

830
01:11:08.699 --> 01:11:11.117
Guess the wolf's out of the bag.

831
01:11:16.123 --> 01:11:20.001
Alice, is it possible that everything
is true?

832
01:11:20.711 --> 01:11:23.087
The fairy tales and horror stories?

833
01:11:23.171 --> 01:11:26.716
Is it possible that there isn't anything
sane or normal at all?

834
01:11:28.885 --> 01:11:30.803
Hey, l think we should go back
and see if Jacob's okay.

835
01:11:30.887 --> 01:11:33.514
l hope Paul sinks some teeth in him.
Serves him right.

836
01:11:33.598 --> 01:11:35.391
No way. Jacob's a natural.

837
01:11:35.475 --> 01:11:39.186
You see him phase on the fly?
l got five says Paul doesn't touch him.

838
01:11:39.271 --> 01:11:41.731
Come on in, Bella. We won't bite.

839
01:11:42.065 --> 01:11:43.816
Speak for yourself.

840
01:11:45.027 --> 01:11:46.986
l done me wrong

841
01:11:47.070 --> 01:11:49.280
And done all wrong

842
01:11:50.490 --> 01:11:53.492
All the wrong I’ve done
I’m sure I’ll live quite long

843
01:11:53.577 --> 01:11:58.164
Oh, hey, about Emily, Sam's fiancée?
Don't stare. It bugs Sam.

844
01:12:00.792 --> 01:12:02.501
Why would l stare?

845
01:12:02.586 --> 01:12:05.671
Are you guys hungry? Like l have to ask.

846
01:12:13.096 --> 01:12:14.680
Who's this?

847
01:12:14.765 --> 01:12:16.599
Bella Swan. Who else?

848
01:12:18.268 --> 01:12:19.310
Hmm.

849
01:12:19.394 --> 01:12:21.645
So, you're the vampire girl.

850
01:12:24.691 --> 01:12:26.776
So, you're the wolf girl.

851
01:12:29.613 --> 01:12:31.030
Guess so.

852
01:12:31.114 --> 01:12:33.699
Well, I’m engaged to one.

853
01:12:37.037 --> 01:12:41.582
Save some for your brothers.
And ladies first. Muffin?

854
01:12:42.626 --> 01:12:44.085
Sure. Thanks.

855
01:12:44.169 --> 01:12:47.671
Leave it to Jacob to find a way
around Sam's gag order.

856
01:12:48.465 --> 01:12:50.383
He didn't say anything to me.

857
01:12:50.467 --> 01:12:51.634
That's a wolf thing.

858
01:12:51.718 --> 01:12:54.220
Alpha's orders get obeyed
whether we want them to or not.

859
01:12:54.304 --> 01:12:56.555
And check it out.
We can hear each other's thoughts.

860
01:12:56.640 --> 01:13:00.476
Would you shut up?
These are trade secrets. Damn it!

861
01:13:00.811 --> 01:13:03.145
This chick runs with vampires.

862
01:13:04.147 --> 01:13:06.732
You can't really run with vampires.

863
01:13:08.693 --> 01:13:10.569
'Cause they're fast.

864
01:13:10.821 --> 01:13:13.572
Yeah? Well, we're faster.

865
01:13:14.991 --> 01:13:16.659
Freaked out yet?

866
01:13:18.370 --> 01:13:20.746
You're not the first monsters I’ve met.

867
01:13:20.831 --> 01:13:23.666
Jake's right. You're good with weird.

868
01:13:25.460 --> 01:13:26.627
Hey.

869
01:13:46.022 --> 01:13:47.356
Sorry.

870
01:14:01.830 --> 01:14:03.706
So you're a werewolf?

871
01:14:05.500 --> 01:14:07.877
Yeah. Last time l checked.

872
01:14:10.130 --> 01:14:13.215
A few lucky members
of the tribe have the gene.

873
01:14:13.550 --> 01:14:17.386
A bloodsucker moves into town
and the fever sets in.

874
01:14:19.973 --> 01:14:21.056
Mono.

875
01:14:22.809 --> 01:14:24.351
Yeah. l wish.

876
01:14:27.606 --> 01:14:31.692
Well, can't you find a way to just stop?

877
01:14:34.237 --> 01:14:36.238
l mean, it's wrong.

878
01:14:38.825 --> 01:14:41.368
It’s not a lifestyle choice, Bella.

879
01:14:41.786 --> 01:14:44.497
l was born this way. l can't help it.

880
01:14:44.581 --> 01:14:47.750
You're such a hypocrite. What,
I’m not the right kind of monster for you?

881
01:14:47.834 --> 01:14:49.752
It’s not what you are.

882
01:14:50.170 --> 01:14:53.547
It’s what you do. They never hurt anybody.

883
01:14:55.967 --> 01:14:57.384
You've killed people, Jake.

884
01:14:57.469 --> 01:14:59.887
Bella, we're not killing anyone.

885
01:15:01.932 --> 01:15:03.349
Then who is?

886
01:15:03.433 --> 01:15:06.393
What we're trying
to protect you people from,

887
01:15:06.645 --> 01:15:08.771
the only thing we do kill,

888
01:15:11.149 --> 01:15:12.441
vampires.

889
01:15:13.944 --> 01:15:15.027
Wait, Jake, you can't.

890
01:15:15.111 --> 01:15:17.363
Don't worry.
We can't touch your little precious Cullens

891
01:15:17.447 --> 01:15:19.907
unless they violate the treaty.

892
01:15:20.450 --> 01:15:22.618
That's not what I’m saying.

893
01:15:22.911 --> 01:15:25.454
You can't kill vampires. They'll...

894
01:15:25.956 --> 01:15:27.623
They'll kill you.

895
01:15:27.791 --> 01:15:31.210
Really? We took out that leech
with the dreads easy enough.

896
01:15:35.632 --> 01:15:36.757
Laurent?

897
01:15:36.841 --> 01:15:39.510
And his red-headed girlfriend is next.

898
01:15:39.970 --> 01:15:41.345
Victoria's here?

899
01:15:41.429 --> 01:15:44.431
Was. We chased her all the way
to the Canadian border the other night.

900
01:15:44.516 --> 01:15:47.935
She keeps coming back.
We don't know what she's after.

901
01:15:48.019 --> 01:15:49.353
l do.

902
01:15:52.732 --> 01:15:53.857
Me.

903
01:16:02.993 --> 01:16:05.828
Don't worry. We've got this place covered.

904
01:16:06.496 --> 01:16:08.956
She won't get near you or Charlie.

905
01:16:09.499 --> 01:16:11.250
Look, you've got to be careful.

906
01:16:11.334 --> 01:16:14.420
She's fast. You don't know how fast she is.

907
01:16:14.504 --> 01:16:18.382
You know, your lack of confidence in us
is a little insulting.

908
01:16:19.884 --> 01:16:21.760
All right, I’d better go.

909
01:16:23.138 --> 01:16:24.680
You gotta go?

910
01:16:25.599 --> 01:16:26.765
Yeah.

911
01:16:27.517 --> 01:16:29.643
Got a vampire to kill.

912
01:16:43.283 --> 01:16:45.826
Alice, I’m all right.

913
01:16:47.495 --> 01:16:49.246
Until I’m alone.

914
01:16:50.540 --> 01:16:53.000
And lately, that's all the time.

915
01:16:53.418 --> 01:16:56.128
Jacob's gone. He's hunting Victoria.

916
01:16:56.212 --> 01:16:58.464
And Charlie's hunting Jacob.

917
01:16:58.548 --> 01:17:00.215
And you're gone.

918
01:17:01.217 --> 01:17:02.968
And so is Edward.

919
01:17:06.973 --> 01:17:09.350
And there's just nothing now.

920
01:17:12.395 --> 01:17:14.396
You got something, Harry?

921
01:17:15.607 --> 01:17:17.232
Nope. Nothing.

922
01:17:24.908 --> 01:17:26.825
But l realize where l have to go,

923
01:17:26.910 --> 01:17:29.453
what l have to do to see him again.

924
01:17:41.257 --> 01:17:43.801
A tear in my brain

925
01:17:49.265 --> 01:17:52.893
Allows the voices in

926
01:17:59.275 --> 01:18:02.611
They wanna push you off the path

927
01:18:07.325 --> 01:18:10.828
With their frequency wires

928
01:18:18.253 --> 01:18:21.964
And you can do no wrong

929
01:18:28.263 --> 01:18:34.810
In my eyes

930
01:18:37.021 --> 01:18:40.524
You can do no wrong

931
01:18:46.781 --> 01:18:53.495
In my eyes

932
01:18:55.457 --> 01:18:57.499
A drunken salesman

933
01:18:57.584 --> 01:18:59.501
Your hearing damage

934
01:18:59.586 --> 01:19:01.462
Your mind is restless

935
01:19:01.546 --> 01:19:03.630
They say you're getting better

936
01:19:03.715 --> 01:19:06.967
But you don't feel any better

937
01:19:14.058 --> 01:19:16.101
Your speakers are blowing

938
01:19:16.186 --> 01:19:18.270
Your ears are wrecking

939
01:19:18.354 --> 01:19:20.272
Your hearing damage

940
01:19:20.356 --> 01:19:24.860
You wish you felt better

941
01:19:32.952 --> 01:19:36.705
You can do no wrong

942
01:19:42.879 --> 01:19:52.888
In my eyes

943
01:20:27.423 --> 01:20:28.966
Don't do this.

944
01:20:33.930 --> 01:20:36.056
You wanted me to be human.

945
01:20:38.560 --> 01:20:39.893
Watch me.

946
01:20:42.647 --> 01:20:43.939
Please.

947
01:20:45.233 --> 01:20:46.233
For me.

948
01:20:46.317 --> 01:20:48.986
You won't stay with me any other way.

949
01:20:51.698 --> 01:20:53.615
Bella, please.

950
01:21:56.095 --> 01:22:02.517
This constant noise all the time

951
01:22:12.987 --> 01:22:18.867
Even though you're the only one l see

952
01:22:21.829 --> 01:22:23.080
Breathe!

953
01:22:24.832 --> 01:22:25.874
Breathe!

954
01:22:27.543 --> 01:22:29.586
Come on, Bella, breathe!

955
01:22:36.678 --> 01:22:39.304
Bella? Bella, can you hear me?

956
01:22:45.645 --> 01:22:47.020
Jake?

957
01:22:48.439 --> 01:22:49.856
Come here.

958
01:22:55.238 --> 01:22:57.614
What the hell were you thinking?

959
01:22:58.741 --> 01:23:00.951
l just wanted to see something.

960
01:23:01.411 --> 01:23:05.122
Get her home!
I’m gonna go help out over at Harry's place.

961
01:23:08.126 --> 01:23:10.168
What happened at Harry's?

962
01:23:10.420 --> 01:23:13.088
Harry Clearwater had a heart attack.

963
01:23:13.756 --> 01:23:16.341
Charlie and my dad
are over at his place with his family.

964
01:23:16.426 --> 01:23:17.926
Is he okay?

965
01:23:20.096 --> 01:23:21.430
He's gone.

966
01:23:25.143 --> 01:23:28.687
Come on. I’ll get you something dry
and drive you home.

967
01:23:39.866 --> 01:23:42.451
1 08 degrees over here.

968
01:23:44.328 --> 01:23:45.537
God!

969
01:23:46.664 --> 01:23:48.623
My hands are freezing.

970
01:23:50.752 --> 01:23:53.295
It must be nice, never getting cold.

971
01:23:53.629 --> 01:23:55.338
It’s a wolf thing.

972
01:23:56.132 --> 01:23:57.466
It’s not.

973
01:23:58.134 --> 01:23:59.968
It’s a Jacob thing.

974
01:24:00.470 --> 01:24:02.304
You're just warm.

975
01:24:04.682 --> 01:24:06.641
You're like your own sun.

976
01:24:10.229 --> 01:24:13.940
This is better, now that you know about me.

977
01:24:17.278 --> 01:24:18.487
But...

978
01:24:23.785 --> 01:24:26.161
You saw what happened to Emily.

979
01:24:29.499 --> 01:24:31.083
Sam got angry.

980
01:24:32.001 --> 01:24:34.211
Lost it for a split second.

981
01:24:35.630 --> 01:24:37.714
Em was standing too close.

982
01:24:40.134 --> 01:24:42.844
He'll never be able to take that back.

983
01:24:45.473 --> 01:24:47.516
What if l got mad at you?

984
01:24:58.945 --> 01:25:00.403
Sometimes,

985
01:25:02.990 --> 01:25:05.534
l feel like I’m gonna disappear.

986
01:25:12.125 --> 01:25:14.376
Okay, not that you need me

987
01:25:15.044 --> 01:25:17.379
to tell you something like this,

988
01:25:19.006 --> 01:25:22.592
but l always will.
You're not gonna lose yourself.

989
01:25:25.513 --> 01:25:27.681
l wouldn't let that happen.

990
01:25:29.934 --> 01:25:31.184
How?

991
01:25:34.647 --> 01:25:36.940
I’ll tell you all the time

992
01:25:40.570 --> 01:25:42.571
how special you are.

993
01:26:02.049 --> 01:26:04.259
Thank you. For everything.

994
01:26:11.309 --> 01:26:12.475
Wait.

995
01:26:15.271 --> 01:26:16.980
There's a vampire.

996
01:26:17.440 --> 01:26:19.149
How do you know?

997
01:26:19.400 --> 01:26:22.444
l can smell it. I’m getting you out of here.

998
01:26:23.279 --> 01:26:24.821
That's Carlisle's car.

999
01:26:26.365 --> 01:26:27.866
They're here.

1000
01:26:28.242 --> 01:26:31.786
Bella, it's a trick! Stop!
You gotta come with me!

1001
01:26:35.333 --> 01:26:36.958
They won't hurt me.

1002
01:26:37.043 --> 01:26:40.462
lf a Cullen is back here,
this is their territory.

1003
01:26:40.880 --> 01:26:43.298
Treaty says we can only defend
on our own lands.

1004
01:26:43.382 --> 01:26:47.469
-l can't protect you here.
-Okay. That's okay. You don't have to.

1005
01:26:49.972 --> 01:26:51.723
You're about to cross a line.

1006
01:26:51.807 --> 01:26:53.725
Then don't draw one.

1007
01:26:54.018 --> 01:26:55.310
Please?

1008
01:27:12.203 --> 01:27:13.411
Alice?

1009
01:27:13.704 --> 01:27:16.289
-Oh, my God! What are you...
-Bella!

1010
01:27:16.916 --> 01:27:21.086
I’m sorry, l just,
l can't believe you're here. Is...

1011
01:27:21.170 --> 01:27:24.506
Would you like to explain to me
how you're alive?

1012
01:27:25.216 --> 01:27:26.258
What?

1013
01:27:26.342 --> 01:27:29.511
l saw a vision of you. You jumped off a cliff.

1014
01:27:30.471 --> 01:27:32.597
Why in the hell
would you try and kill yourself?

1015
01:27:32.682 --> 01:27:33.807
l mean, what about Charlie?

1016
01:27:33.891 --> 01:27:36.643
-What about...
-l didn't try to kill myself.

1017
01:27:36.727 --> 01:27:38.186
I was cliff jumping.

1018
01:27:38.271 --> 01:27:40.021
Recreationally.

1019
01:27:40.106 --> 01:27:41.523
It was fun.

1020
01:27:43.734 --> 01:27:47.737
l have never met anyone
more prone to life-threatening idiocy.

1021
01:27:53.244 --> 01:27:54.369
Does...

1022
01:27:54.912 --> 01:27:56.955
Did you tell him?

1023
01:27:57.039 --> 01:27:58.123
No.

1024
01:27:59.792 --> 01:28:02.544
He only calls in once every few months.

1025
01:28:04.130 --> 01:28:06.381
He said he wants to be alone.

1026
01:28:12.221 --> 01:28:15.598
Bella, what is that
God-awful wet dog smell?

1027
01:28:17.059 --> 01:28:18.059
Um...

1028
01:28:18.894 --> 01:28:20.645
That's probably me.

1029
01:28:21.647 --> 01:28:23.898
Or it's Jacob.

1030
01:28:25.151 --> 01:28:26.568
Jacob who?

1031
01:28:27.903 --> 01:28:30.030
Jacob's kind of a werewolf.

1032
01:28:31.615 --> 01:28:34.743
Bella!
Werewolves are not good company to keep.

1033
01:28:36.037 --> 01:28:37.912
Speak for yourself.

1034
01:28:42.752 --> 01:28:44.919
l had to see you were safe.

1035
01:28:46.464 --> 01:28:49.257
l thought you couldn't protect me here.

1036
01:28:49.508 --> 01:28:51.259
Guess l don't care.

1037
01:28:54.972 --> 01:28:57.265
Well, I’m not gonna hurt her.

1038
01:28:58.851 --> 01:29:00.769
No, you're just a harmless Cullen.

1039
01:29:00.853 --> 01:29:04.272
I’m talking about the other bloodsucker
who tried to kill Bella because of you.

1040
01:29:04.357 --> 01:29:05.398
Victoria?

1041
01:29:05.483 --> 01:29:07.609
Yeah, Victoria's been around.

1042
01:29:07.693 --> 01:29:09.444
l didn't see her.

1043
01:29:09.945 --> 01:29:13.490
l didn't see you
get pulled out of the water, either.

1044
01:29:14.408 --> 01:29:17.369
l can't see past you and your pack of mutts.

1045
01:29:17.453 --> 01:29:19.579
Don't get me upset...

1046
01:29:19.663 --> 01:29:23.833
-Hey, stop. Stop, stop, stop, stop.
-...or things are gonna get very ugly.

1047
01:29:29.215 --> 01:29:31.132
I’ll give you a minute.

1048
01:29:37.139 --> 01:29:38.223
Hey.

1049
01:29:39.308 --> 01:29:41.893
You're not going anywhere.
You're gonna come back,

1050
01:29:41.977 --> 01:29:44.771
-right?
-As soon as you put the dog out.

1051
01:29:53.781 --> 01:29:55.156
Is he...

1052
01:29:59.286 --> 01:30:00.829
Are there others?
How many Cullens are here

1053
01:30:00.913 --> 01:30:03.081
and how long are they staying?

1054
01:30:03.165 --> 01:30:04.290
No.

1055
01:30:05.167 --> 01:30:06.918
It’s just Alice.

1056
01:30:11.549 --> 01:30:14.342
And she can stay as long as she'd like.

1057
01:30:16.804 --> 01:30:19.139
Well, are the rest coming back?

1058
01:30:25.438 --> 01:30:26.521
No.

1059
01:30:28.357 --> 01:30:29.774
Not that l know of.

1060
01:30:30.985 --> 01:30:32.527
Anything else?

1061
01:30:36.824 --> 01:30:38.199
That's it.

1062
01:30:40.369 --> 01:30:44.038
Well, if that's all,
then you'd better go run back to Sam.

1063
01:30:47.126 --> 01:30:48.918
I’ve done it again.

1064
01:30:49.879 --> 01:30:52.046
l keep breaking my promise.

1065
01:30:57.303 --> 01:31:00.054
We don't have to do this to each other.

1066
01:31:04.518 --> 01:31:06.060
Yes, we do.

1067
01:31:17.907 --> 01:31:19.240
Bella...

1068
01:31:42.139 --> 01:31:43.765
Swan residence.

1069
01:31:49.522 --> 01:31:51.606
He's not here right now.

1070
01:31:52.316 --> 01:31:54.234
He's arranging a funeral.

1071
01:32:10.167 --> 01:32:11.793
Who was that?

1072
01:32:12.086 --> 01:32:13.127
What?

1073
01:32:13.212 --> 01:32:15.004
Always in the way.

1074
01:32:17.174 --> 01:32:18.383
Who was that?

1075
01:32:18.467 --> 01:32:20.093
Bella, step back.

1076
01:32:20.177 --> 01:32:23.388
-Jake, who was that?
-Bella! Bella, it's Edward.

1077
01:32:23.973 --> 01:32:27.392
He thinks you're dead.
Rosalie told him why l came here.

1078
01:32:29.603 --> 01:32:32.313
Why would you...
Why didn't you let me speak to him?

1079
01:32:32.398 --> 01:32:33.565
-He didn't ask for you.
-Bella.

1080
01:32:33.649 --> 01:32:37.235
-l don't care!
-Bella. Bella! He's going to the Volturi.

1081
01:32:37.903 --> 01:32:39.821
He wants to die, too.

1082
01:32:41.740 --> 01:32:44.867
He left you, Bella.
He didn't want you anymore. Remember?

1083
01:32:44.952 --> 01:32:48.413
No, I’m not gonna let him kill himself
out of guilt.

1084
01:32:49.123 --> 01:32:50.957
What about your dad?

1085
01:32:51.500 --> 01:32:54.877
I’m 1 8.
I’m legally free to go, and l left a note.

1086
01:32:56.672 --> 01:32:58.381
Please, Bella,

1087
01:32:59.842 --> 01:33:01.926
just stay here.

1088
01:33:03.679 --> 01:33:05.179
For Charlie.

1089
01:33:08.017 --> 01:33:09.559
Or for me.

1090
01:33:10.603 --> 01:33:12.145
l have to go.

1091
01:33:18.110 --> 01:33:19.861
I’m begging you.

1092
01:33:22.531 --> 01:33:23.906
Please.

1093
01:33:25.659 --> 01:33:27.285
Goodbye, Jacob.

1094
01:33:35.794 --> 01:33:37.003
Okay.

1095
01:33:45.137 --> 01:33:47.430
)

1096
01:34:38.440 --> 01:34:40.775
So you've made up your minds.

1097
01:34:41.026 --> 01:34:43.486
I’m afraid your particular gifts

1098
01:34:44.613 --> 01:34:46.948
are too valuable to destroy.

1099
01:34:47.908 --> 01:34:52.787
But if you're unhappy with your lot, join us.

1100
01:34:53.914 --> 01:34:57.625
We would be delighted to utilize
your skills.

1101
01:34:58.585 --> 01:35:01.129
Won't you consider staying with us?

1102
01:35:02.923 --> 01:35:05.258
You know it will happen anyway.

1103
01:35:05.342 --> 01:35:07.260
Not without cause.

1104
01:35:11.515 --> 01:35:13.099
Such a waste.

1105
01:35:20.315 --> 01:35:22.108
I’m guessing you didn't rent this car?

1106
01:35:22.192 --> 01:35:24.235
l figured you wouldn't be opposed
to grand theft auto.

1107
01:35:24.319 --> 01:35:25.695
Not today.

1108
01:35:29.032 --> 01:35:30.700
What? What do you see?

1109
01:35:30.784 --> 01:35:32.660
They refused him.

1110
01:35:32.745 --> 01:35:35.163
-So?
-He's gonna make a scene.

1111
01:35:35.497 --> 01:35:38.332
-Show himself to the humans.
-No! When?

1112
01:35:39.376 --> 01:35:42.420
He's gonna wait until noon,
when the sun's at its highest.

1113
01:35:45.174 --> 01:35:46.382
God, Alice, you got to hurry up.

1114
01:35:46.467 --> 01:35:48.342
There's Volterra.

1115
01:36:13.118 --> 01:36:15.953
-Why are they all in red?
-San Marco's Day festival.

1116
01:36:16.038 --> 01:36:18.831
They're commemorating
the expulsion of vampires from the city.

1117
01:36:18.916 --> 01:36:20.249
It’s the perfect setting.

1118
01:36:20.334 --> 01:36:22.877
The Volturi will never let him get far enough
to reveal himself.

1119
01:36:22.961 --> 01:36:24.670
We have five minutes.

1120
01:36:24.755 --> 01:36:27.048
l know, Bella, just breathe.

1121
01:36:33.138 --> 01:36:34.138
Alice!

1122
01:36:34.223 --> 01:36:36.390
Bella, you're the only one
he can't see coming.

1123
01:36:36.475 --> 01:36:39.560
lf l go, he'll read my thoughts.
He'll think I’m lying. He'll rush into it.

1124
01:36:40.312 --> 01:36:43.648
-Where do l go?
-He'll be under the clock tower. Go!

1125
01:38:36.094 --> 01:38:37.428
Don't!

1126
01:38:39.514 --> 01:38:40.640
Heaven.

1127
01:38:40.724 --> 01:38:42.391
You have to move.

1128
01:38:43.226 --> 01:38:46.020
Open your eyes. Look at me. I’m alive.

1129
01:38:46.772 --> 01:38:48.522
You have to move.

1130
01:38:49.358 --> 01:38:50.608
Bella.

1131
01:38:58.075 --> 01:39:00.201
-You're here.
-I’m here.

1132
01:39:03.038 --> 01:39:04.246
You're alive.

1133
01:39:07.709 --> 01:39:08.918
Yes.

1134
01:39:18.387 --> 01:39:20.972
l needed to make you see me once.

1135
01:39:22.015 --> 01:39:23.307
You had to know that l was alive,

1136
01:39:23.392 --> 01:39:26.519
that you didn't have
to feel guilty about anything.

1137
01:39:29.398 --> 01:39:31.983
l can let you go now.

1138
01:39:36.738 --> 01:39:38.906
l never acted out of guilt.

1139
01:39:41.368 --> 01:39:44.870
l just couldn't live in a world
where you don't exist.

1140
01:39:46.248 --> 01:39:48.290
-But you said...
-l lied.

1141
01:39:49.001 --> 01:39:52.086
l had to lie. But you believed me so easily.

1142
01:39:57.759 --> 01:40:01.345
Because it doesn't make sense
for you to love me.

1143
01:40:04.057 --> 01:40:07.643
l mean, I’m nothing. I’m human. I’m nothing.

1144
01:40:08.854 --> 01:40:12.440
Bella, you're everything to me.

1145
01:40:14.401 --> 01:40:16.110
You're everything.

1146
01:40:41.803 --> 01:40:43.888
l won't be needing your services after all,
gentlemen.

1147
01:40:43.972 --> 01:40:46.057
Aro wants to speak with you again.

1148
01:40:46.141 --> 01:40:47.391
No rules were broken.

1149
01:40:47.476 --> 01:40:51.645
Nonetheless, we should take this
conversation to a more appropriate venue.

1150
01:40:51.730 --> 01:40:52.980
Fine.

1151
01:40:54.316 --> 01:40:56.650
Bella, why don't you go
and enjoy the rest of the festival?

1152
01:40:56.735 --> 01:40:58.069
The girl comes with us.

1153
01:40:58.153 --> 01:40:59.862
No. You can go to hell.

1154
01:41:02.240 --> 01:41:03.824
Come on, guys.

1155
01:41:04.076 --> 01:41:07.495
It’s a festival.
You wouldn't want to make a scene.

1156
01:41:08.330 --> 01:41:09.747
We wouldn't.

1157
01:41:10.123 --> 01:41:11.457
Enough.

1158
01:41:13.001 --> 01:41:14.168
Jane.

1159
01:41:14.961 --> 01:41:17.963
Aro sent me to see what was taking so long.

1160
01:41:26.014 --> 01:41:27.973
Just do as she says.

1161
01:41:40.529 --> 01:41:41.904
Go ahead.

1162
01:41:45.909 --> 01:41:47.576
Don't be scared.

1163
01:41:48.537 --> 01:41:49.870
Are you?

1164
01:41:50.831 --> 01:41:51.914
No.

1165
01:42:30.495 --> 01:42:32.621
-Is she human?
-Yes.

1166
01:42:35.792 --> 01:42:37.418
Does she know?

1167
01:42:37.919 --> 01:42:39.086
Yes.

1168
01:42:39.421 --> 01:42:41.213
Then, why would...

1169
01:42:42.841 --> 01:42:44.633
She wants to be.

1170
01:42:45.093 --> 01:42:46.510
And so she will be.

1171
01:42:46.595 --> 01:42:48.012
Or dessert.

1172
01:42:56.521 --> 01:43:00.316
Sister. They send you out to get one
and you bring back two.

1173
01:43:01.067 --> 01:43:02.526
And a half.

1174
01:43:03.695 --> 01:43:05.070
Such a clever girl.

1175
01:43:05.155 --> 01:43:07.072
What a happy surprise!

1176
01:43:08.116 --> 01:43:10.784
Bella is alive after all.

1177
01:43:11.661 --> 01:43:14.330
Isn't that wonderful?

1178
01:43:15.457 --> 01:43:17.333
l love a happy ending.

1179
01:43:18.460 --> 01:43:19.418
Ah.

1180
01:43:21.796 --> 01:43:23.631
They are so rare.

1181
01:43:30.472 --> 01:43:32.973
Her blood appeals to you so much

1182
01:43:34.267 --> 01:43:36.101
it makes me thirsty.

1183
01:43:36.353 --> 01:43:39.146
How can you stand to be so close to her?

1184
01:43:39.314 --> 01:43:42.316
-It’s not without difficulty.
-Yes, l can see that.

1185
01:43:42.400 --> 01:43:43.609
)

1186
01:43:45.737 --> 01:43:49.323
Aro can read every thought
I’ve ever had with one touch.

1187
01:43:50.325 --> 01:43:52.534
And now you know everything.

1188
01:43:53.161 --> 01:43:54.954
So get on with it.

1189
01:43:58.083 --> 01:44:01.293
You are quite a soul reader yourself,
Edward.

1190
01:44:02.921 --> 01:44:07.174
Though you can't read Bella's thoughts.

1191
01:44:10.595 --> 01:44:12.054
Fascinating.

1192
01:44:15.600 --> 01:44:20.980
l would love to see
if you are an exception to my gifts, as well.

1193
01:44:23.692 --> 01:44:25.859
Would you do me the honor?

1194
01:44:46.715 --> 01:44:48.132
Interesting.

1195
01:44:48.508 --> 01:44:49.508
Hmm.

1196
01:44:50.302 --> 01:44:51.885
l see nothing.

1197
01:45:01.229 --> 01:45:02.771
l wonder if...

1198
01:45:03.606 --> 01:45:06.567
Let us see if she's immune
to all our powers.

1199
01:45:08.153 --> 01:45:09.611
Shall we, Jane?

1200
01:45:11.489 --> 01:45:13.240
-No!
-Pain.

1201
01:45:29.257 --> 01:45:30.591
Stop!

1202
01:45:31.426 --> 01:45:33.177
Stop! Please! Stop!

1203
01:45:33.261 --> 01:45:37.097
Stop! Just stop hurting him!
Please! Please!

1204
01:45:38.808 --> 01:45:40.059
Jane?

1205
01:45:42.145 --> 01:45:43.145
Master?

1206
01:45:47.734 --> 01:45:49.443
Go ahead, my dear.

1207
01:45:54.949 --> 01:45:57.159
This may hurt just a little.

1208
01:46:13.301 --> 01:46:14.802
Remarkable!

1209
01:46:17.013 --> 01:46:19.264
She confounds us all.

1210
01:46:20.308 --> 01:46:23.477
So what do we do with you now?

1211
01:46:24.020 --> 01:46:27.147
You already know
what you're going to do, Aro.

1212
01:46:28.149 --> 01:46:29.983
She knows too much.

1213
01:46:30.527 --> 01:46:32.319
She's a liability.

1214
01:46:33.655 --> 01:46:34.655
Hmm.

1215
01:46:36.282 --> 01:46:37.825
That's true.

1216
01:46:41.704 --> 01:46:42.996
Felix?

1217
01:46:46.876 --> 01:46:47.960
No!

1218
01:47:49.522 --> 01:47:52.608
Please! No! No! Please, please!

1219
01:47:55.487 --> 01:47:58.614
Kill me! Kill me! Not him.

1220
01:48:09.626 --> 01:48:12.169
How extraordinary.

1221
01:48:13.880 --> 01:48:18.300
You would give up your life
for someone like us.

1222
01:48:19.427 --> 01:48:20.761
A vampire.

1223
01:48:22.180 --> 01:48:24.598
A soulless monster.

1224
01:48:24.682 --> 01:48:26.683
Just get away from her!

1225
01:48:30.772 --> 01:48:35.234
You don't know a thing about his soul.

1226
01:48:46.829 --> 01:48:48.539
This is a sadness.

1227
01:48:50.667 --> 01:48:54.253
lf only it were your intention
to give her immortality.

1228
01:49:03.137 --> 01:49:04.429
Wait!

1229
01:49:06.057 --> 01:49:08.141
Bella will be one of us.

1230
01:49:09.852 --> 01:49:11.353
I’ve seen it.

1231
01:49:13.147 --> 01:49:15.065
I’ll change her myself.

1232
01:49:48.975 --> 01:49:50.475
Mesmerizing.

1233
01:49:50.893 --> 01:49:55.314
To see what you have seen
before it has happened.

1234
01:49:58.234 --> 01:50:02.696
Your gifts will make for an intriguing

1235
01:50:03.948 --> 01:50:05.365
immortal,

1236
01:50:06.451 --> 01:50:07.993
Isabella.

1237
01:50:12.874 --> 01:50:14.291
Go now.

1238
01:50:15.001 --> 01:50:16.960
Make your preparations.

1239
01:50:17.754 --> 01:50:19.755
Let us be done with this.

1240
01:50:21.591 --> 01:50:23.884
Heidi will arrive any moment.

1241
01:50:25.720 --> 01:50:29.139
Thank you for your visit.

1242
01:50:29.223 --> 01:50:30.766
We will return the favor.

1243
01:50:30.850 --> 01:50:33.810
l would advise that you follow through
on your promise soon.

1244
01:50:33.895 --> 01:50:36.229
We do not offer second chances.

1245
01:50:37.899 --> 01:50:40.984
Goodbye, my young friends.

1246
01:50:47.367 --> 01:50:49.159
Nice fishing, Heidi.

1247
01:50:49.243 --> 01:50:51.495
Yes, they do look rather juicy.

1248
01:50:51.579 --> 01:50:53.288
Save some for me.

1249
01:50:54.248 --> 01:50:57.084
This way, please. Stay together.

1250
01:51:11.724 --> 01:51:13.266
Stop! Stop!

1251
01:51:24.112 --> 01:51:25.654
You're here.

1252
01:51:27.699 --> 01:51:29.282
You can sleep.

1253
01:51:33.079 --> 01:51:35.706
I’ll still be here when you wake up.

1254
01:51:39.293 --> 01:51:42.337
Bella, the only reason l left

1255
01:51:44.132 --> 01:51:47.050
was because l thought
l was protecting you.

1256
01:51:48.928 --> 01:51:50.554
l needed you

1257
01:51:50.638 --> 01:51:54.599
to have a chance at a normal, happy life.

1258
01:51:58.688 --> 01:52:01.064
It was so easy for you to leave.

1259
01:52:03.651 --> 01:52:07.320
Leaving you was the hardest thing
I’ve done in 1 00 years.

1260
01:52:14.120 --> 01:52:15.662
And l swear,

1261
01:52:16.998 --> 01:52:19.666
l will never fail you again.

1262
01:52:21.961 --> 01:52:23.503
I’m so sorry.

1263
01:52:25.923 --> 01:52:27.841
-Charlie's coming.
-Hey.

1264
01:52:31.012 --> 01:52:32.387
You okay?

1265
01:52:33.806 --> 01:52:35.056
I’m fine.

1266
01:52:38.186 --> 01:52:40.353
Dad, you don't have to worry.

1267
01:52:40.855 --> 01:52:42.856
You know, last time you said that,
you took off.

1268
01:52:42.940 --> 01:52:45.108
l didn't see you for three days.

1269
01:52:46.819 --> 01:52:48.695
I’m really sorry, Dad.

1270
01:52:50.490 --> 01:52:54.201
Bella, do not ever do that to me again.

1271
01:52:57.038 --> 01:52:58.121
Ever.

1272
01:53:00.917 --> 01:53:02.501
And you're grounded

1273
01:53:02.960 --> 01:53:05.086
for the rest of your life.

1274
01:53:06.255 --> 01:53:07.422
Okay.

1275
01:53:17.725 --> 01:53:20.519
I’m not technically
breaking any of his rules.

1276
01:53:23.523 --> 01:53:26.733
He did say
l couldn't take a step inside the door.

1277
01:53:27.235 --> 01:53:29.528
l came in through the window.

1278
01:53:33.157 --> 01:53:35.659
He's not gonna forgive me easily.

1279
01:53:38.120 --> 01:53:39.412
l know.

1280
01:53:41.457 --> 01:53:42.833
Can you?

1281
01:53:46.587 --> 01:53:48.171
l hope you can,

1282
01:53:48.965 --> 01:53:52.175
'cause l honestly don't know
how to live without you.

1283
01:53:56.514 --> 01:53:57.931
Come here.

1284
01:54:15.575 --> 01:54:18.535
Once Alice changes me,

1285
01:54:21.455 --> 01:54:23.623
you can't get rid of me.

1286
01:54:24.834 --> 01:54:27.127
She won't need to change you.

1287
01:54:27.753 --> 01:54:31.256
There are always ways
to keep the Volturi in the dark.

1288
01:54:32.967 --> 01:54:35.343
No. No.

1289
01:54:42.143 --> 01:54:44.144
You all know what l want.

1290
01:54:46.314 --> 01:54:49.316
And l know how much I’m asking for.

1291
01:54:51.569 --> 01:54:55.071
The only thing that l can think of
for it to be fair is to just vote.

1292
01:54:55.156 --> 01:54:58.491
-You don't know what you're talking about.
-Shut up.

1293
01:55:00.119 --> 01:55:01.328
Alice?

1294
01:55:01.787 --> 01:55:04.331
l already consider you my sister.

1295
01:55:08.127 --> 01:55:09.753
-Yes.
-Thank you.

1296
01:55:09.837 --> 01:55:11.338
l vote "yes."

1297
01:55:12.757 --> 01:55:16.259
It would be nice to not
want to kill you all the time.

1298
01:55:18.137 --> 01:55:19.137
Hmm.

1299
01:55:19.263 --> 01:55:20.597
I’m sorry.

1300
01:55:22.516 --> 01:55:25.644
I’m really sorry to both of you
for how I've acted,

1301
01:55:26.270 --> 01:55:28.313
and I’m really grateful
that you were brave enough

1302
01:55:28.397 --> 01:55:30.523
to go and save my brother.

1303
01:55:32.026 --> 01:55:35.487
But this isn't a life
l would have chosen for myself.

1304
01:55:38.032 --> 01:55:41.701
And l wish that there'd been someone
to vote "no" for me.

1305
01:55:44.580 --> 01:55:45.997
So, no.

1306
01:55:47.416 --> 01:55:49.334
I vote "Hell, yeah."

1307
01:55:51.212 --> 01:55:53.588
And we can pick a fight
with these Volturi some other way.

1308
01:55:53.673 --> 01:55:56.633
I already consider you a part of the family.

1309
01:55:57.259 --> 01:55:58.510
Yes.

1310
01:56:04.392 --> 01:56:06.601
Why are you doing this to me?

1311
01:56:08.312 --> 01:56:09.646
You know what this means.

1312
01:56:09.730 --> 01:56:13.608
You've chosen not to live without her,
which leaves me no choice.

1313
01:56:14.360 --> 01:56:16.236
I won't lose my son.

1314
01:56:22.451 --> 01:56:26.496
I’ll wait until after graduation
to make it easier on Charlie.

1315
01:56:31.502 --> 01:56:34.421
Edward, I want you to be the one to do it.

1316
01:56:41.429 --> 01:56:43.513
He wants to talk to me.

1317
01:56:46.642 --> 01:56:48.268
So you're still alive for now.

1318
01:56:48.352 --> 01:56:50.812
He thinks it's me keeping
you away.

1319
01:56:50.896 --> 01:56:53.398
You stay the hell out of my head.

1320
01:56:54.483 --> 01:56:57.986
Jacob, I know you have something
to say to me.

1321
01:57:00.322 --> 01:57:04.242
But l want to say something to you first,
if that's all right.

1322
01:57:05.369 --> 01:57:06.786
Thank you.

1323
01:57:09.915 --> 01:57:13.293
Thank you for keeping Bella alive
when I didn't.

1324
01:57:13.836 --> 01:57:15.962
No. You didn't.

1325
01:57:17.965 --> 01:57:20.592
And it wasn't for your benefit, trust me.

1326
01:57:20.676 --> 01:57:22.552
I’m still grateful.

1327
01:57:23.137 --> 01:57:24.345
But I’m here now.

1328
01:57:24.430 --> 01:57:27.140
I’m not gonna leave her side
until she orders me away.

1329
01:57:27.224 --> 01:57:28.558
We'll see.

1330
01:57:31.437 --> 01:57:33.605
Hey, my turn to talk.

1331
01:57:38.152 --> 01:57:41.696
I’m here to remind you
about a key point in the treaty.

1332
01:57:41.864 --> 01:57:43.740
I haven't forgotten.

1333
01:57:43.824 --> 01:57:45.366
What key point?

1334
01:57:45.618 --> 01:57:47.911
lf any of them bites a human,

1335
01:57:48.662 --> 01:57:50.455
the truce is over.

1336
01:57:51.832 --> 01:57:53.666
But if I choose it,
it has nothing to do with you.

1337
01:57:53.751 --> 01:57:55.794
No. No, I won't let you.

1338
01:57:57.379 --> 01:57:59.798
You're not gonna be one of them, Bella.

1339
01:57:59.882 --> 01:58:01.800
It’s not up to you.

1340
01:58:02.510 --> 01:58:04.844
You know what we'll do to you.
I won't have a choice.

1341
01:58:04.929 --> 01:58:06.596
Bella, please, come.

1342
01:58:06.680 --> 01:58:07.847
Wait.

1343
01:58:09.850 --> 01:58:12.435
Is he gonna hurt me? Read his mind.

1344
01:58:19.777 --> 01:58:21.111
Jake,

1345
01:58:27.535 --> 01:58:29.160
I love you.

1346
01:58:33.874 --> 01:58:35.542
So, please,

1347
01:58:40.089 --> 01:58:42.173
don't make me choose,

1348
01:58:47.930 --> 01:58:49.889
'cause it'll be him.

1349
01:58:53.227 --> 01:58:55.103
It’s always been him.

1350
01:59:02.570 --> 01:59:03.903
Bella...

1351
01:59:11.704 --> 01:59:14.831
-Goodbye, Jacob.
-No, you don't speak for her!

1352
01:59:19.587 --> 01:59:21.588
Bella, get out of here.

1353
01:59:23.382 --> 01:59:24.757
Stop!

1354
01:59:26.927 --> 01:59:28.219
Stop!

1355
01:59:28.304 --> 01:59:31.389
You can't hurt each other
without hurting me.

1356
01:59:50.409 --> 01:59:51.534
Jake.

1357
02:00:06.592 --> 02:00:08.009
He's right.

1358
02:00:09.136 --> 02:00:11.596
You shouldn't become what l am.

1359
02:00:16.477 --> 02:00:18.478
I can't do this alone.

1360
02:00:21.148 --> 02:00:23.107
Then, please, just wait.

1361
02:00:30.115 --> 02:00:32.742
Just give me five years.

1362
02:00:38.332 --> 02:00:39.999
That's too long.

1363
02:00:44.463 --> 02:00:45.922
Then three?

1364
02:00:50.636 --> 02:00:52.428
You're so stubborn.

1365
02:00:54.306 --> 02:00:56.391
What are you waiting for?

1366
02:01:05.150 --> 02:01:08.194
l have one condition

1367
02:01:10.698 --> 02:01:13.157
if you want me to do it myself.

1368
02:01:17.288 --> 02:01:19.122
What's the condition?

1369
02:01:19.707 --> 02:01:21.416
And then forever.

1370
02:01:23.210 --> 02:01:25.086
That's what I’m asking.

1371
02:01:36.432 --> 02:01:38.099
Marry me, Bella.

1372
02:04:12.671 --> 02:04:16.549
White demon love song down the hall

1373
02:04:18.218 --> 02:04:22.555
White demon shadow on the road

1374
02:04:23.765 --> 02:04:27.894
Back up your mind, there is a call

1375
02:04:29.271 --> 02:04:32.982
He isn't coming after all

1376
02:04:33.066 --> 02:04:35.276
Love this time

1377
02:04:35.360 --> 02:04:39.530
She likes the way he sings

1378
02:04:40.365 --> 02:04:44.327
White demon love song's in her dreams

1379
02:04:48.582 --> 02:04:52.793
White demon, where's your selfish kiss?

1380
02:04:54.087 --> 02:04:58.466
White demon sorrow will arrange

1381
02:04:59.635 --> 02:05:03.804
Let's not forget about the fear

1382
02:05:05.098 --> 02:05:10.520
Black invitation to this place
that cannot change

1383
02:05:10.604 --> 02:05:15.816
While strangely holy

1384
02:05:16.068 --> 02:05:19.278
Come for a rain

1385
02:05:24.785 --> 02:05:29.830
White demon, widen your heart's scope

1386
